{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse","id":244557,"title":"[Recruitment] Rage Across the Delaware Valley- Werewolf: the Apocalypse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-29T22:59:09-07:00","id":244557,"title":"[Recruitment] Rage Across the Delaware Valley- Werewolf: the Apocalypse","content":"It\u2019s been quite a while since I\u2019ve had the chance to run an Old World of Darkness game. Or are we supposed to call it the Classic World of Darkness now? I suppose that it doesn\u2019t really matter; I never warmed to the nWoD games, so the original World of Darkness has always been the only World of Darkness for me.<br /> <br /> Rage Across the Delaware Valley, along with its cousin Philadelphia by Night, is a setting I first wrote when I was in college (back, of course, when the original World of Darkness was in print) and used for a few games on campus, and from which I\u2019ve sampled bits and pieces along the way. I recently came across a few scattered remnants of my old notes, and was inspired to update the setting and try running a game again. So, through the collection of the few pieces of my notes that remain, along with painstaking recollections, I have endeavored to reconstruct, update and (I hope) improve the setting.<br /> <br /> My schedule these days, as my friends and family can attest, is highly erratic. A steady tabletop game, or even a steady Skype or chat game, would be virtually impossible for me to run. I simply could not commit to being regularly available at the same time every week, and I would not put a dedicated gaming group through the unpleasantness of never being certain whether I would be joining them from week to week. A PBEM or PbP game, on the other hand, is something that I can easily handle given my current workload. So, here I am and, being that I\u2019m in more of a Werewolf than a Vampire mood at the moment, I bring you Rage Across the Delaware Valley.<br /> <br /> Below I will provide the basic information of the setting, information that would be available with minimal effort to any player character in the chronicle. It can be treated as IC information by all players, but should not be assumed to be 100% accurate! This represents information that is generally known or assumed by the Garou of the Delaware Valley, and some of it is flat out wrong. Before I get into setting information, however, let\u2019s discuss some general information about the game.<br /> <br /> For starters, this is a game of Werewolf: the Apocalypse. There will be crossover with some of the other games of the oWoD, but this is W:tA. No players will be playing Vampire or Changeling or Mage characters. The cosmology will be W:tA based, with a few interesting tidbits cherry-picked from the other games. The Vampire NPCs in the setting may believe in silly things like Noddist Lore, but they\u2019re dead wrong. If we were playing Philadelphia by Night, it might be a different story.<br /> <br /> That being said, I\u2019m a big fan of Exalted, and I\u2019ve always liked the idea of the Exalted setting as a precursor to the oWoD. So, Exalted fans might pick out the occasional easter egg referring to Exalted history, or bits and pieces of the deep cosmology of the game if players dig deep enough will have ties to Exalted, but it isn\u2019t going to be a huge, essential part of the story, for the most part. It\u2019s just there to amuse me and my fellow Exalted fans. And I promise, no actual Exalted NPCs will appear. ;-)<br /> <br /> Oh, and for the record, I\u2019m not a big fan of Demon: the Fallen (nothing wrong with it, I just never got into it and I don\u2019t have the books), so don\u2019t expect anything from D:tF to appear in the game at all, not even background. It never happened. Every other oWoD game is fair game for me to use for background material at the very least, but no Demon.<br /> <br /> Now, I understand that some Hunter: the Reckoning supplements had some relatively detailed information about Philadelphia as a setting. I have nothing against H:tR, but I don\u2019t own those particular supplements, and am not going to be using that information. So, if you have an idea of what Philadelphia and the Delaware Valley look like in the canon oWoD from H:tR (or other canon sources, for that matter), don\u2019t expect Rage Across Delaware Valley to look like that.<br /> <br /> OK, now that that\u2019s settled, let\u2019s talk rules for a minute. We will primarily be using the W20 core book for our rules. Players without access to that material can get by with the revised core book- if any contradictions come up, we\u2019ll resolve them and move on. That said, there are many gifts, rites, etc. from numerous revised sourcebooks that I am perfectly OK with, but if you intend to use such things, take a sec to run them by me first. Most times, I\u2019ll just approve them or maybe tweak them a little to my satisfaction, but it\u2019s still good to know. If it is from an earlier edition than revised\u2026 well, I\u2019ll still say yes to anything reasonable, but more tweaking might be required.<br /> <br /> As far as in character timing goes, the first chapter of the game will begin on January 1, 2014, just after midnight, and will progress forward IC depending on how fast things move along. I\u2019m a big fan of downtime blue-booking, so there will be jumps forward in between chapters.<br /> <br /> As far as the W:tA metaplot goes, I\u2019ll be cherry-picking which aspects of the metaplot did and did not happen. My decisions about a few of the more significant events and individuals, from the W:tA perspective, are included in the sidebar below. If you have a question about a specific piece of metaplot and would like to know whether it did or did not happen, ask. However, if it is something that a new character in this game could not possibly know, I may not answer and simply let you discover the truth for yourself as the game goes on, if it becomes relevant (for example, there\u2019s no way any starting character would know if the extermination of the Tremere Antitribu happened in this setting).<br /> <br /> <u>Metaplot Sidebar</u><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u>Week of Nightmares</u>- The Week of Nightmares did happen, in July of 1999. Even a decade and a half later, the exact details of what happened are not widely known, but it is still seen as a sign of the impending Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> <u>Red Star</u>- The Red Star, Anthelios, did appear to the Garou on July 15, 1999, during the Week of Nightmares, and still shines in the Umbral sky. Garou observers still claim that it is coming closer to Earth, but it seems to have slowed down steadily over the years. It is still not generally visible from the physical world, but individuals with special senses (including certain gifts) can see it. While average mortals cannot see it, it has been detected by certain astronomic devices. The fact that it has not yet been confirmed visibly continues to baffle scientists. The scientific name for the phenomenon is \u201c2001KX76,\u201d and it was first discovered by mortals in May of 2001. It gets occasional mention in scientific journals as more outlandish theories are put forward to account for its odd behavior, but its significance is not understood by humanity.<br /> <br /> <u>Perfect Metis</u>- The Perfect Metis has <i>not</i> been born. The prophecies that seem to refer to the Perfect Metis are extremely obscure in my setting, and very few Garou are aware of them. The prophecies themselves are ambiguous, seeming to state that the Perfect Metis may appear, and that if it does it will play a significant role in the Apocalypse for good or ill, but that such an appearance is not guaranteed, that the Apocalypse can happen without the Perfect Metis being born and that whether he is born or not depend on a number of other obscure conditions.<br /> <br /> <u>Stargazers</u>- The Stargazers have left the Garou Nation and returned to their ancestral homeland of Tibet, joining the Beast Courts of the Emerald Mother en masse. There are still a handful of individual Stargazers left in the west, but the overwhelming majority of them have gone to the Hengeyokai.<br /> <br /> <u>Samuel Haight</u>- Yeah, he existed. Yeah, he\u2019s still dead. And because it amuses me, his soul is still an ashtray.<br /> <br /> <u>Zhyzhak</u>- She exists, and she\u2019s just as scary now as she was in the original source material. Maybe even scarier. The prophecy about her crushing the \u201cLast Gaian King\u201d under her heel is slowly spreading throughout the Garou nation and becoming general knowledge. And speaking of him\u2026<br /> <br /> <u>Albrecht</u>- Still alive, still the King of House Wyrmfoe, still has the Silver Crown, still insufferably self-righteous.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Now that that\u2019s settled, let\u2019s talk characters. I am ideally looking for 5 PCs to form a pack, but I\u2019m willing to start with 4 if I can\u2019t find 5 players. 6 is the most I am prepared to deal with. 7 would be a little too much for me, though I MIGHT change my mind about that under the right circumstances. All players must play Garou.<br /> <br /> Let me say that again- <i>all players must play Garou</i>. I will not allow Fera player characters of any type, for any reason, nor will I allow kin player characters or crossover player characters from other oWoD games. I\u2019m sorry if that disappoints anyone. There will be Fera NPCs in the game, but this is going to be a story of a Garou pack, not a mixed group of shifters. So, no matter how good your idea is for a Fera character, my answer is going to be \u201cno.\u201d So, please, don\u2019t even ask. Not even the Nuwisha disguised as a Ragabash.<br /> <br /> All twelve extant tribes of Gaian Garou in the Western Concordat are playable. That\u2019s the Black Furies, Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, Fianna, Get of Fenris, Glass Walkers, Red Talons, Shadow Lords, Silent Striders, Silver Fangs, Uktena and Wendigo. I will also allow no more than one player to play a Stargazer if (s)he has a good character background and story. No extinct tribes (Bunyip, Croatan or White Howlers), no Ronin, no Skin Dancers, no Siberakh and definitely no Black Spiral Dancers. And no crazy impossible combos, like Homid Red Talons, or non-Metis male Black Furies. Now, I would like to get a mix of tribes, so I don\u2019t want more than two player characters from the same tribe, though I may make exceptions to this guideline on a case by case basis for very good stories.<br /> <br /> All three breeds are available, without restrictions (except as noted above, vis-\u00e0-vis Homid Red Talons and the like). Even if we end up with an entire pack of the same breed, so be it. I\u2019ll not force players to create characters of different breeds to balance the pack. Players who want to play Metis, do not expect to ignore your character\u2019s deformity, or the social stigma of being a Metis- these things <i>must</i> be role played. I generally prefer physical deformities to psychological ones, but I won\u2019t insist on that. I am also very open to working with you to develop custom deformities, so feel free to ask.<br /> <br /> All five auspices are available. Ideally, I would like to have at least one character of each auspice, but I will not force players to adopt certain roles. As long as we are not completely overloaded with a single auspice, I\u2019ll let the chips fall where they may. Just bear in mind that a wide range of skillsets would be useful. :-) Also, remember that the auspices aren\u2019t straitjackets. There\u2019s no reason that a character can\u2019t be of one auspice while having some personality traits considered appropriate or stereotypical of a different auspice. A person is more complex than a set of lunar-derived personality traits, after all. Of course, if you insist on having astrological justification for your characters non-auspice personality quirks, feel free to delve into Garou astrology for additional depth in this area. A theurge with a surfeit of warrior-type traits may have been born under the sign of Nerigal or Rorg, while a philodox with a trickster nature may have undergone her first change while Mitanu was ascendant. I love Garou astrology. ;-)<br /> <br /> The game will begin with all of the characters going on their rite of passage together (yes, Werewolf fans, I know a multi-tribal Rite of Passage is slightly unusual- it will be explained in character). So, characters will be created using standard W20 rules as if they were Rank 1 Garou, even though they <i>technically</i> won\u2019t be until after they complete their Rite of Passage in Chapter 1. This also means relatively young characters. For Homids, the First Change usually takes place between the ages of 10-16. Earlier is practically unheard of (and I wouldn\u2019t allow a character that young anyway), but the change can be delayed for any number of reasons, both physical and spiritual. There is also a period of training and preparation after the First Change but before the Rite of Passage, which would naturally take longer for a younger Homid. So, to put it bluntly, I would like most of the characters to be in their mid to late teens (15-19). One or two slightly older characters would be acceptable, but anything over 21 or 22 would be pushing it. A character in their early teens might also be possible, but I would need to talk seriously with the player of such a prospective character to make sure that everything would work out OK. 13 is the absolute youngest age for a Homid player character that I am willing to accept. Metis and Lupus characters obviously mature at different rates, so we\u2019ll work out the approximate physical age of the humanoid forms of such characters during character creation, though the above general guidelines will apply.<br /> <br /> I would love to hear character proposals and ideas. What I do <i>not</i> want is to be presented with a completed character sheet before we\u2019ve even discussed the character. I am a very hands-on ST, especially when it comes to character creation, and I prefer to be involved in the process. So, tell me what kind of character you\u2019re thinking about, we\u2019ll work through the details together, and THEN you can write up your sheet. For ease of reference, we\u2019ll all use the same format for our character sheets, which I will present in a later post, when we get to the point that we need them.<br /> <br /> The game will be based, as the name implies, in the Delaware Valley. The pack\u2019s adventures will take them around the world and throughout the umbra, but their home sept(s) will be in the Delaware Valley. The Delaware Valley, for our purposes, comprises Philadelphia, South East Pennsylvania, South Jersey and northern Delaware. Characters do not necessarily need to be native to this area (though it would be nice if at least some of them were), but if they are from off, there needs to be a reason why they ended up here. That can be as simple as their tribe choosing to foster them with a sept in the Delaware Valley, but I\u2019m willing to work with everyone to come up with plausible, interesting and workable reasons for your characters to be here.<br /> <br /> I like variety among the characters. I like healthy conflict within the pack. Irreconcilable differences are a whole other matter. However good a character concept is, if I am convinced it would inevitably lead to the self-destruction of the pack (or, worse, the rest of the pack ganging up on and expelling or killing the character in question), I will not allow it. So, please, don\u2019t come with a character who has a pathological hatred of Silver Fangs and has an unshakeable desire to kill all Silver Fangs in their sleep if we already have two Silver Fang characters. Red Talons probably deserve special mention here. I <i>like</i> Red Talons. I hope someone decides to play a Red Talon. Red Talons can make fascinating characters and a great addition to many packs. The stereotypical Red Talon who wants to wipe out every human on the planet (such as, for example, a diehard member of the Lodge of the Predator Kings) is not that kind of Red Talon, though. So, please, if you want to play a Red Talon, don\u2019t play into that stereotype.<br /> <br /> One more thing I should mention. The game, as I said, is starting with the characters\u2019 Rite of Passage. If all goes well, we all enjoy ourselves and the game continues, it will proceed until the characters earn their way to Rank 5, at which point they will be major players in the Apocalypse itself. So, if all goes well, this game will continue until the world ends. ;-) It is, therefore, very important to make sure that the characters you create are characters that you are going to enjoy playing long term. I hope that\u2019s something we can work together on.<br /> <br /> I have in mind a series of four major stories that will weave together into one chronicle- the first story will cover the character\u2019s rite of passage and take them to about rank 2 or 3, with the PCs becoming respected among the local Garou (I hope). The second story will see them through to about rank 4, and will see them become major players in the Delaware Valley, with their fame starting to spread to other regions. The third story will bring them to rank 5 (or, possibly, rank 6 if the circumstances dictate, but I\u2019m not planning on that happening) and will see the PCs ranking among the leaders of their tribes, recognized all over the world. This will set the characters up to take a leadership role for the fourth story, which will culminate the narrative of the chronicle with the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> I think that covers the basics. I\u2019ll post later with more specifics about the mechanics of character creation, including a few house rules, but this should be enough for now to get you guys thinking and proposing character concepts.<br /> <br /> My next post, as promised, will contain general information about the setting itself. As character creation goes on, each player will receive more specific information, mostly via private message, about the setting from the perspective of their particular tribe, but what follows will be information that can be considered generally known to all the cubs.<br /> <br /> I should probably apologize about the length of this first post. I suppose that it might be a little intimidating. :-) I can be verbose at times. I hope I didn\u2019t scare anyone away. I know that there are a lot of great role players on this forum, and a lot of Old World of Darkness enthusiasts, too. I know that there are also people on this forum who have never played any oWoD games, and are here because they\u2019re Exalted or Scion or Trinity or nWoD fans.<br /> <br /> I hope, with this game, to make something that is fun and accessible for all these types of players. So, if you\u2019re a W:tA aficionado and are nostalgic for that old time game of savage horror, here you are. If you\u2019ve never played Werewolf: the Apocalypse before, but are curious to try something new, here you are.<br /> <br /> I hope we can have some fun as we come together to find the answer to that timeless question:<br /> <br /> <i>When will you rage?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":". 08-30-2014, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T23:01:28-07:00","id":244563,"title":"","content":"<u>Basic Setting Information- Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <br /> Here now is the basic information for the setting of Rage Across the Delaware Valley. As I noted before, this is information that should be considered generally available with minimal effort for any player character, and can be considered IC knowledge for each. In other words, this information is commonly known or assumed by the majority of the Garou of the Delaware Valley. <i>Do not assume that this information is 100% accurate</i>. I am telling you, flat out, OOC, that some of this information is right, some is wrong and most is incomplete.<br /> <br /> As we progress with character creation, I will communicate with each player some more specific knowledge that their characters have access to by virtue of their backgrounds, home septs and tribal affiliations. Some of it will contradict the general information contained here, as different tribes have different ideas about what is going on, and why. Your characters must decide for themselves what, if anything, they believe.<br /> <br /> Please note also that I am running a game, not writing a sourcebook. I am not making an attempt to create an exhaustive treatment of the supernatural history of Philadelphia and its surroundings. Nor am I writing a paper on the history of Philadelphia, Delaware and South Jersey. This is a brief overview only. There are a great many more details of the setting, some of which will become apparent as the game goes on, and some of which will remain mysterious.<br /> <br /> As with any RP setting, I am not trying to present a 100% factually accurate view of the region. A great many details will be different in the interest of creating what I hope is a more interesting game and setting. So, players who happen to be from the Delaware Valley (as I am), or who are familiar with the region, don\u2019t be surprised to find details about the area are different in the game when compared to real life.<br /> <br /> <u>A [Very] Brief Overview of Certain Garou Historical Highlights</u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Prior to the arrival of the Europeans (or \u201cWyrmbringers,\u201d if you prefer), what we call the Delaware River Valley was part of the heartland of the Leni Lenape nation. The Lenape were kinfolk of the Croatan tribe, and the caerns in the region were tended to and protected by the Croatan. When the Croatan sacrificed themselves to stop Eater of Souls, the Wendigo and Uktena tried to move into their former territory, to protect the Croatan lands and tend their caerns. The Delaware Valley was much closer to Wendigo lands than Uktena lands, so it was largely Wendigo who travelled to the area.<br /> <br /> The Wendigo, however, focused largely on the area north of the Delaware Valley, such as the lands of the Iroquois (who had also been Croatan kinfolk). As a result, the Delaware Valley had very few native Garou protectors when the European Garou began to arrive. A number of Croatan caerns were completely abandoned, and even the larger ones that the Wendigo had sent packs to were suffering from the lack of care. The European Garou used this situation to their advantage, pushing the Wendigo out of the territories and taking over the former Croatan caerns for themselves.<br /> <br /> Between the appropriated Croatan caerns and a few newly constructed ones, the Delaware Valley was able to support a larger than average Garou population (see the note below the caern listing for more on this phenomenon). Over time, the Children of Gaia and the Glass Walkers tended to be the most influential tribes of the region.<br /> <br /> In the late 1990s, something happened to the Shadow Lords of the Sept of the Thundering Pines. The details still aren\u2019t completely clear, but somehow the garou of the sept (and the nearby Piney Sept of the Bone Gnawers) became tainted, falling to the service of the Wyrm. They kept this secret for several years, working clandestinely with the local Black Spiral Dancers, causing harm to the Gaian cause wherever they could. Over time, the other local garou, especially the Silver Fangs of the Sept of the New World\u2019s Glory, began to suspect that something was wrong and started to investigate.<br /> <br /> Knowing that their secret would soon be out, the tainted Shadow Lords and their Black Spiral Dancer allies made plans for a devastating sneak attack, and waited for a sign. When a Red Star appeared in the sky, they knew their sign had come. They revealed their taint to the world by attacking the Fairmount Sept during a moot. Wiping out the entire Sept except for a single kin survivor, the act kicked off a war that lasted for twelve years. If a garou in the Delaware Valley mentions \u201cthe war,\u201d this is the conflict to which she is referring.<br /> <br /> Every other Sept in the Delaware Valley became involved in the struggle. Many nomadic packs travelled to the region to lend aid, and a number of allied septs from outside the area sent packs to help as well. The tide truly turned, however, when several packs of powerful Shadow Lords travelled from their homeland in Eastern Europe to join the war on the side of the Gaian Garou and destroy their fallen tribemates. Eventually, the war was won. The Caern of the Thundering Pines was cleansed and reclaimed, the tainted Shadow Lords were destroyed to the last werewolf and the Black Spiral Dancers forced back into their holes.<br /> <br /> It has been three years since the fighting stopped, and the region\u2019s Garou are still recovering. The Fairmount caern is still inactive, every attempt to reopen it having failed. Two caerns in Delaware that were lost remain lost, and many packs that go seeking them do not return. Most of the packs from afar that traveled to the region to aid in the fight have returned home, though some chose to remain and make their home here. The one good thing that came of the war was a renewed sense of cooperation among the Garou of the Delaware Valley, as the septs forced to work closely together for their very survival now work to maintain those close ties.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <u>Active Caerns</u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u>Sept of the Thundering Pines</u><br /> Level: 4<br /> Type: Stamina<br /> Totem: Thunderbird<br /> Tribal Structure: Open, Shadow Lord led<br /> Location: Wharton State Forest, New Jersey Pine Barrens<br /> Notes: Once one of the most powerful Croatan caerns, the Sept of the Thundering Pines was taken by the Shadow Lords when they came to the New World. The Shadow Lord sept that had been controlling and \u201cprotecting\u201d the caern somehow became corrupted by the Wyrm. Joining with the local Black Spiral Dancers, they attacked the other local septs of the Delaware Valley in a devastating surprise attack during a time known as the \u201cWeek of Nightmares\u201d in 1999, destroying the Fairmount Sept and precipitating a war that lasted for over a decade. With the corrupt Shadow Lords finally defeated, the caern was reclaimed by other Shadow Lords from around the world who came to put down their tainted brethren and cleanse the caern. The past three years have been spent cleansing every last vestige of the taint, bringing the caern back to Gaia in full and helping the garou of the entire Delaware Valley to heal after the devastating conflict.<br /> <br /> <u>Sept of the New World\u2019s Glory</u><br /> Level: 4<br /> Type: Willpower<br /> Totem: Eagle<br /> Tribal Structure: Silver Fang controlled, open to others by invitation<br /> Location: French Creek State Park, Pennsylvania<br /> Notes: The Caern of the New World\u2019s Glory claims the distinction of being the first caern that the Europeans actually built in the New World, instead of stealing from the native Garou. It is an important stronghold of the Silver Fangs, and is the ancestral home of an influential family of House Wyrmfoe, the Dawnstars, who have passed leadership of the caern through their lineage for centuries.<br /> <br /> <u>Marshall Island Sept</u><br /> Level: 3<br /> Type: Humor<br /> Totem: Dana<br /> Tribal Structure: Open, primarily Fianna and Children of Gaia, traditionally led by Fianna<br /> Location: Treasure Island Scout Reservation, Point Pleasant, Pennsylvania<br /> Notes: Located on the unused portions of an island that is part of a Boy Scout Reservation in the Delaware River, the Marshall Island Sept has been multi-tribal since its inception. Traditionally led by the Fianna, but with a strong Children of Gaia presence and representation from numerous other tribes, the Marshall Island Sept was a beacon of cooperation in the Delaware Valley, especially after the fall of the Unity caern at Fairmount Park. It is said that the Fae have a stronghold of their own nearby, and that the Marshall Island Sept has friendly relations with these \u201cchangelings,\u201d including oaths of mutual defense.<br /> <br /> <u>Blessed Harvest Sept</u><br /> Level: 3<br /> Type: Plenty<br /> Totem: Corn Maiden<br /> Tribal Structure: Children of Gaia controlled, open to others by invitation<br /> Location: Salisbury Township, Lancaster County, PA<br /> Notes: Located in the farmlands of Lancaster County, the garou of the Blessed Harvest Sept have made pacts with the native spirits of agriculture, nurturing both Gaia and the local human population. It is said that some of the Children of Gaia of this sept are part of a local camp that advocates a lifestyle based on that of the Amish, rejecting advanced technology to be closer to Gaia, but if that is true they seldom leave their own territory.<br /> <br /> <u>Sept of Dockyard Miracles</u><br /> Level: 2<br /> Type: Stealth<br /> Totem: Flea<br /> Tribal Structure: Bone Gnawers controlled, open to others by invitation<br /> Location: Waterfront, Camden, NJ<br /> Notes: Impossible to find without the help of its Bone Gnawer keepers, the stealthy caern claims the entire Camden Waterfront as its bawn. Originally a closed sept, the Bone Gnawers began allowing outsiders into their territory during the war with the corrupt Shadow Lords. A base of operations that the Wyrm could not locate was invaluable, and many packs owed their lives to the Sept\u2019s timely efforts to rescue and hide them from pursuers. Besides earning the appreciation (if not always the respect) of the other septs in the Delaware Valley for their efforts, the Bone Gnawers of this sept are still known as important information brokers.<br /> <br /> <u>Society Hill Sept</u><br /> Level: 2<br /> Type: Streetwise<br /> Totem: Clashing Boom Boom<br /> Tribal Structure: Open, Glass Walker controlled<br /> Location: Society Hill Hotel, Society Hill neighborhood, Center City, Philadelphia, PA<br /> Notes: After the fall of the Fairmount Sept and the disappearance of the New Castle Sept, the Society Hill Sept became the most important Glass Walker stronghold in the Delaware Valley. Built around an inn/bar in the wealthy and historic Society Hill neighborhood, the important structures of the caern are said to be underground. It is also said that the caern itself has become overcrowded, with too many Glass Walkers present for the caern to easily support. Despite its small size, it was said to be an important strategic location during the war with the corrupt Shadow Lords, housing a powerful transportation fetish of some kind that helped turn the tide. The leader of the sept is an ailing old Glass Walker Mafioso who is not expected to live much longer.<br /> <br /> <u>Sept of Iron Visions</u><br /> Level: 1 (Formerly 3)<br /> Type: Gnosis<br /> Totem: Stourbridge Lion<br /> Tribal Structure: Glass Walkers, open to others by invitation<br /> Location: A now abandoned rail yard in South Philadelphia, PA<br /> Notes: A small sept built around the train yard where a powerful locomotive spirit appeared to the Glass Walkers almost 200 years ago, this caern has been steadily losing power for decades. A single Glass Walker pack work to stave off its destruction. The caern was briefly lost to the tainted Shadow Lords during the conflict with them, but was recovered and cleansed without any permanent damage being done.<br /> <br /> <u>Sept of Friends</u><br /> Level: 1<br /> Type: Calm<br /> Totem: Unicorn<br /> Tribal Structure: Open, Children of Gaia controlled<br /> Location: Frankford Friends Meeting House, Frankford, Philadelphia, PA<br /> Notes: The Quakers (also known as the \u201cSociety of Friends\u201d) of the Delaware Valley had long numbered Children of Gaia kinfolk among their number. The Frankford Friends Meeting House is the oldest surviving meeting house in Philadelphia. The Children of Gaia have seamlessly integrated the caern\u2019s functions into those of the building, which is still used as for Quaker meetings and as a community center.<br /> <br /> <u>Germantown Volunteers Sept</u><br /> Level: 1<br /> Type: Courage<br /> Totem: Boar<br /> Tribal Structure: Open, Get of Fenris dominated<br /> Location: Old Fire Station, Germantown, Philadelphia, PA<br /> Notes: Built around the first volunteer fire station in Germantown (which was not then a part of Philadelphia). The building, which takes most of the block, is still a functioning fire house (now absorbed into the Philadelphia Fire Department). All the fire fighters assigned to the station are kin, primarily of the Get of Fenris, but including a few Uktena, Glass Walkers, Fianna and Bone Gnawers as well. Even the occasional Garou joins for a time, though their Rage makes it difficult for them to be involved in such pursuits. The caern incorporates the entire block, which includes a bar right behind the station where the firefighters go to drink after their shifts.<br /> <br /> <u>Cohanzick Sept</u><br /> Level: 1<br /> Type: Memory<br /> Totem: North Wind<br /> Tribal Structure: Closed, Wendigo Only<br /> Location: Cohanzick Tribal Grounds, Fairton, NJ<br /> Notes: Built very recently on land that was reclaimed by the Nanticoke Leni Lenape Tribal Nation as the Cohanzick Tribal Grounds. The Wendigo and their kin assisted in this reclamation, especially since the area apparently included a small, lost caern that once belonged to the Croatan. Once the land was back in tribal hands, the Wendigo reopened the caern and have protected it fiercely.<br /> <br /> <u>Sept of the Mother\u2019s Needles</u><br /> Level: Unknown<br /> Type: Unknown<br /> Totem: Unknown<br /> Tribal Structure: Closed, Black Furies Only<br /> Location: Brendan T. Byrn State Forest (Formerly Lebanon State Forest), New Jersey Pine Barrens<br /> Notes: The only remaining Black Fury stronghold of note in the Delaware Valley, very little is known about this caern. The Furies emphatically refuse to allow outsiders into their caern. Practically nothing is generally known about this caern beyond the mere fact of its existence, and the fact that it dates back to the time of the Croatan. The Black Fury refusal of outsiders has led to increased friction between them and the local Wendigo, who would like very much to visit the ancient Croatan site.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <u>Wait a minute, that\u2019s a <i>lot</i> of caerns\u2026</u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Yes, it is, and it gets worse if you look down and see the list of defunct caerns. As has always been their custom, the writers of White Wolf were careful not to specify how many caerns a particular area should hold, or a definitive number for the garou population. The idea was that an area had as many caerns as the ST wanted it to have, according to the needs of the setting. However, by any standard, the Delaware Valley has a LOT of caerns.<br /> <br /> This is not an oversight, and this is not ST fiat. The Garou of the Delaware Valley are aware that there is something unusual about the area. There <i>should not be</i> this many caerns here. However, despite centuries of occupation, no modern Garou knows why there are so many caerns in the local area. Perhaps the Croatan knew, but if so, that secret died with them. There are plenty of theories, but with no definitive answer to the riddle forthcoming, the local Garou generally don\u2019t think about it anymore, simply accepting it as a quirk of the local land and umbra that wellsprings of spiritual energy allowing for the creation of caerns are more common than usual here.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure it\u2019s nothing to worry about. ;-)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <u>Defunct Caerns</u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u>Fairmount Sept</u><br /> Level: 0 (Formerly 4)<br /> Type: Unity<br /> Totem: Duck<br /> Tribal Structure: Was open, traditionally led by Children of Gaia and Glass Walkers<br /> Location: Fairmount Park, West Philadelphia, PA<br /> Notes: Built in massive Fairmount Park in West Philadelphia, the Fairmount Sept was once the center of Garou society in the Delaware Valley. A powerful caern of unity, open to all, it was easily the largest sept in the region. The sept boasted members from all twelve tribes of the Garou Nation (and Stargazers, who at that time had not yet left the west), was frequently visited by individuals and packs from all over the eastern United States and was a beacon of hope and cooperation.<br /> <br /> So, when the tainted Shadow Lords and their Black Spiral Dancer allies made their plans to launch a surprise attack on the Garou of the Delaware Valley, they knew what their first target would be. The appearance of a Red Star in the night sky was the sign they had been waiting for. The fact that the Fairmount Sept was coincidentally holding a moot that very same evening simply made the timing more providential, as if the Wyrm itself had blessed their efforts by making sure that every member of the Sept would be on hand\u2026 and distracted\u2026 for the slaughter.<br /> <br /> Three packs from the Sept of the Thundering Pines and one from the Piney Sept attended the moot, taking advantage of the extreme openness of the caern to infiltrate it. When the time was right, those four packs turned on the caern\u2019s guardians, slaughtering them from within. Then the real attack came, with the rest of the tainted Shadow Lords and dozens of Black Spiral Dancers assaulting the sept simultaneously once the defenders were silenced. There were no garou survivors- only a single young girl, kin to the Children of Gaia, managed to escape, making her way to the Sept of Dockyard Miracles to tell the gruesome tale and expose the corruption of the tainted Shadow Lords, thus beginning the war.<br /> <br /> To make matters worse, the servants of the Wyrm enacted some foul rite, destroying the caern\u2019s spiritual connections in a single night. Twice since then have the local garou attempted to reopen the caern. Both times, the ritemaster literally exploded, and all other participating garou were wracked with pain. Until the source of the problem can be found, the elders of the Delaware Valley have unanimously forbidden any more attempts to reopen the caern. Packs from the Sept of the New World\u2019s Glory, the Society Hill Sept, the Sept of Friends and the Germantown Volunteers Sept take turns patrolling Fairmount Park.<br /> <br /> <u>New Castle Sept</u><br /> Level: 0 (Formerly 3)<br /> Type: Plenty<br /> Totem: Cockroach<br /> Tribal Structure: Was open, Glass Walker controlled<br /> Location: Wilmington, DE<br /> Notes: The largest caern in Delaware and a stronghold of the Glass Walkers, the New Castle Sept was built on the top 5 floors of one of Wilmington\u2019s major office buildings. The Glass Walkers of the sept embraced a corporate culture, dipping their fingers into dozens of industries throughout Delaware, and had frequent confrontations with the local vampires. Despite their local concerns, they still helped to fight threats to the entire region, and participated in the war against the corrupted Shadow Lords. Until they disappeared. One day, without warning, all contact was lost with the sept. Packs that were away from the caern at the time returned to investigate, and were not heard from again. When packs from the other septs of the region tried to make contact, they realized with shock that no one could remember exactly which office building the caern had occupied. Even systematic searches of the office buildings of Wilmington found no evidence that a caern had ever existed. The mystery plagues the Glass Walkers of the Delaware Valley to this day. What could make an entire caern disappear?<br /> <br /> <u>Blue Hole Sept</u><br /> Level: 0 (Formerly 2)<br /> Type: Enigmas<br /> Totem: Bikanaki\u2019hat the Water Keeper, the Great Toad (A water elemental and Lenape spirit)<br /> Tribal Structure: Was open, Population was split between Black Furies, Children of Gaia and Uktena<br /> Location: Winslow Fish and Wildlife Management Area, New Jersey Pine Barrens<br /> Notes: Centered around an unusually clear lake in the Pine Barrens (groundwater in the region is usually tea colored due to the high acidity of the soil), this former Croatan caern was protected by a powerful water elemental. The sept was besieged during the war with the corrupted Shadow Lords; during one of the battles, a pack of Black Spiral Dancers snuck into the caern\u2019s heart and defeated Bikanaki\u2019hat, capturing him in a fetish and carrying him away. The surviving garou of the sept were unable to maintain the caern, reluctantly abandoning the site and moving to other septs when the caern went dormant. It is said that the caern could be reopened if Bikanaki\u2019hat could be rescued and freed from his fetish prison, but all attempts to find him have failed.<br /> <br /> <u>Piney Sept</u><br /> Level: 0 (Formerly 1)<br /> Type: Primal-Urge<br /> Totem: Raccoon<br /> Tribal Structure: Bone Gnawers, was open to others by invitation<br /> Location: Southern Edge of the Wharton State Forest, New Jersey Pine Barrens<br /> Notes: A small sept in a community at the southern edge of the Pine Barrens, the Piney Sept was populated by Bone Gnawers and their kin. The humans of the area were (and are) derided by other residents of New Jersey as \u201cPineys,\u201d considered inbred, backwards, dangerous hicks who flouted society and the law. The Bone Gnawers and kinfolk who lived among this population helped encourage these views, since it tended to keep the authorities from the area, which helped them protect the rare Bone Gnawer wolf kin that also secretly lived near the caern. The Bone Gnawers were closely allied with the Shadow Lords of the Sept of the Thundering Pines. Some say that the Piney Bone Gnawers willingly joined the tainted Shadow Lords in service to the Wyrm; others claim that the Shadow Lords tricked the Bone Gnawers, tainting them in some way by deception or force. Regardless of the truth, the Piney Bone Gnawers (and many of their kin) became tainted, and did fight alongside the Wyrm-corrupted Shadow Lords. Their caern was corrupted during the process, and the land was considered too tainted to reopen as a caern when the battles were finally complete. The community is now a small abandoned village, known to the locals as a ghost town.<br /> <br /> <u>Canaresse Sept</u><br /> Level: 0 (Formerly 1)<br /> Type: Healing<br /> Totem: Bear<br /> Tribal Structure: Was open, primarily populated by Children of Gaia and Fianna<br /> Location: Bombay Hook National Wildlife Refuge, Kent County, Delaware<br /> Notes: Built at a wildlife refuge in the salt marshes, this small sept was devoted primarily to ecological concerns. They tended to concern themselves less with violent solutions and direct confrontation with the forces of corruption and more with healing the damage left by such confrontations and protecting the natural world, even while surrounded by the works of humanity. They did fight when necessary, but their focus on healing instead of combat, and their choice of Bear as their sept totem, did not endear them to many of the other local garou. Regardless, when the caern was attacked in force by Black Spiral Dancers during the war with the corrupted Shadow Lords, the other septs sent packs to their aid, but they were too late, and the caern had already fallen. Since the end of the war, three attempts have been made to reopen the caern. The first and second were met with massive attacks by the forces of the Wyrm, leading to the failure of the ritual. The participants of the third attempt simply disappeared without a trace.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <u>Delaware</u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> You may have noticed that there are no active caerns in Delaware- only two listed as defunct. One of the septs disappeared entirely. The other was destroyed in battle, but one of the groups sent to try to rebuild it disappeared without a trace.<br /> <br /> It is known that there is at least one major Black Spiral Dancer Hive in Delaware, and probably more than one. Packs of Black Spiral Dancers have been chased back to Delaware by garou from the rest of the Delaware Valley, as well as from neighboring Maryland. Once they are inside the state, however, they almost invariably lose their prey, sometimes under circumstances that defy belief. All attempts to locate these hives have failed. Packs and individuals sent into Delaware are frequently ambushed, and sometimes simply disappear. Spirits queried about the situation seem to have no answers. All attempts to investigate have failed- sometimes disastrously. Several septs in Maryland have outright forbidden their younger packs from travelling through Delaware, and some of the Elders in the Delaware Valley septs have spoken of doing the same.<br /> <br /> Something strange is happening in Delaware. Something very strange.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <u>Tribal Presence</u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Black Furies: One of the smaller tribes, the Black Furies have never had a particularly strong presence in the Delaware Valley. Their only major stronghold is the mysterious Sept of the Mother\u2019s Needles, which they keep isolated from all outsiders (this has caused some particular tensions between them and the local Wendigo). Besides this sept, they are present in small numbers at several of the other open septs of the Delaware Valley. They have small numbers of kin throughout the area, including a number located in Bryn Mawr, PA, a number of whom are part of the faculty and staff of Bryn Mawr College.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers: With the death of so many Glass Walkers during the war with the corrupt Shadow Lords, the Bone Gnawers are almost certainly the second largest tribe in the Delaware Valley (after the Children of Gaia). Their numbers have never made them particularly influential though, which is not unusual for them; they are, however, known to be the most well informed Garou of the region. Their only remaining stronghold in the region is the Sept of Dockyard Miracles in Camden, the safest caern in the Delaware Valley- it\u2019s impossible to find unless you already know where it is. They used to have a second sept in the Pine Barrens, where they protected a significant number of their lupine kinfolk, but that sept (for whatever reason) joined with the tainted Shadow Lords and had to be put down. Their role in the war led to increased appreciation for the Bone Gnawers, if not necessarily increased respect. Regardless, the other tribes still sometimes come to them, metaphorical hats in hand, when they need information they can get no where else.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia: The Children of Gaia are almost certainly the largest tribe in the Delaware Valley, and have historically been one of the most influential (alongside the Glass Walkers). Many of them first came to the region with their Quaker kin, and claim to have been in part responsible for the relatively peaceful contact between the European settlers and the Leni Lenape natives. The Wendigo scoff at these claims. In any case, the Children of Gaia control several of the local caerns and have a significant population in a number of caerns that they don\u2019t control. The loss of the Fairmount caern has hurt them deeply, however, and they are at the forefront of attempts to reopen the caern and reestablish the sept. They also work diligently to maintain the close ties between the septs of the Delaware Valley that were established during the course of the war with the corrupt Shadow Lords.<br /> <br /> Fianna: There were a significant number of Fianna kin with each major migration of the Irish to Philadelphia and its surroundings. Most of their kin are in the city itself, and though the Fianna have no strongholds in the city, there are small numbers of them present in the local septs, and they had significant numbers at the now defunct Fairmount Sept. They are the traditional leaders of the Marshall Island Sept, where they are said to have powerful alliances with the local faeries.<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris: The kinfolk of the Get of Fenris, unsurprisingly, were originally settled in Germantown, though they have since spread throughout the region. They are closely allied to the Silver Fangs of the Sept of the New World\u2019s Glory, and there are traditionally several Fenrir members of the sept. They founded the Germantown Volunteers Sept as their kin founded the first volunteer firefighting company of Germantown and have maintained the caern ever since.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers: The Glass Walkers traditionally have been one of the most influential tribes in the Delaware Valley, but they suffered greatly during the war with the tainted Shadow Lords. Many of their tribemates, including most of the local elders, were slaughtered at the Fairmount Sept, and a major caern of theirs in Wilmington, Delaware mysteriously disappeared during the fighting. Another caern of theirs fell, but was reclaimed before permanent damage was done. They lost most of their leadership, and the current leader of their last major stronghold, the Society Hill Sept, is said to be old and failing. Fortunately, their kin populations survived the war largely unharmed, and there has been a slow influx of young Glass Walkers from outside the area, so they are starting to rebuild. Unfortunately, they do not have the space, and the Society Hill Sept is starting to get a little overcrowded. Put simply, the Glass Walkers of the Delaware Valley stand at a crossroads.<br /> <br /> Red Talons: There is only one Red Talon currently known to be living in the Delaware Valley. Sunset Howl is the Galliard of Rorg\u2019s Eyes, an all Lupus pack that was nomadic until coming to the Delaware Valley during the war with the corrupt Shadow Lords. They joined the local Gaian Garou in their struggle and settled down with the new Sept of the Thundering Pines when the fighting stopped, where they have been ever since. There was one Red Talon, a young Ragabash, living in the Fairmount Sept, but she was killed when the sept was wiped out. The Red Talons are known to have a small sept in the Poconos, the Sept of the Hidden Peak. Rumor says they like to eat skiers.<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords: The Shadow Lords established a presence in the Delaware Valley relatively early. Some of the first members of the tribe who came to the New World settled in New Jersey, taking what is now called the Caern of the Thundering Pines as their protectorate. However they came to possess the caern (and accounts differ, especially if you ask the Wendigo), they protected it ably and well for centuries. Until they fell. To this day, nobody knows how or why they fell to the Wyrm; trying to guess the reason and method is a favorite campfire game of young Garou in the region. However it happened, they turned on us all, and needed to be wiped out. The war was long and bloody, and might still be going on if large numbers of Shadow Lords from all over hadn\u2019t come to put down their tainted brethren. After the war, those newcomer Shadow Lords who chose to stay reclaimed the caern for themselves, which the devastated inhabitants of the other septs were happy to let them do, so long as they pledged to keep the structure of the caern open. The elders of the sept are now mostly Eastern European garou who work to restore the honor of their tribe in the Delaware Valley.<br /> <br /> Silent Striders: There is only one Silent Strider currently known to be living in the Delaware Valley. Chases-the-Horizon is the Ahroun and leader of Rorg\u2019s Eyes, an all Lupus pack that was nomadic until coming to the Delaware Valley during the war with the corrupt Shadow Lords. They joined the local Gaian Garou in their struggle and settled down with the new Sept of the Thundering Pines when the fighting stopped, where they have been ever since. Occasionally Silent Striders from other regions pass through the area, delivering messages or portents. There were several other Silent Striders who were part of the Fairmount Sept, but they were killed when the Sept was destroyed. They are said to have had a small community of kin among the city\u2019s middle-eastern population, but no one has kept track of these individuals, assuming they still live.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs: The Silver Fangs have long been a major presence in the Delaware Valley. The Sept of the New World\u2019s Glory claims to have been the first caern built by the Europeans in the New World, rather than appropriated from the Wendigo or Uktena or built on the ruins of an abandoned Croatan site. The validity of this claim is open to debate. In any case, the caern has been in the hands of a single Silver Fang family, the Dawnstars, since it was first founded. The leader of the caern styles himself a \u201cHigh Lord,\u201d and has always been a Dawnstar. The Dawnstars are one of the most prominent (and purely bred) families of House Wyrmfoe, and are staunch supporters of King Albrecht. The caern is currently led by High Lord William Dark-Eye Dawnstar, an old Elder Ahroun who was a renowned warrior in his day. All of his Garou children and several grandchildren have died, however, leaving a single young garou grandchild who has yet to complete their rite of passage to be the heir apparent. It is whispered that most of his descendants died fighting the same foe, a powerful Vampire who wounded William in battle decades ago, giving him the deed name \u201cdark-eye,\u201d when the Silver Fang tried to recover a powerful family heirloom of the Dawnstars (more on that below). There are several families of Silver Fang kin in the Delaware Valley in addition to the Dawnstars, all of whom are tightly monitored by their garou relatives.<br /> <br /> Stargazers: There are almost no Stargazers currently known to be living in the Delaware Valley, and no known community of Stargazer kin. The few that were here in years past left when their tribe relocated to Asia, or died when Fairmount Sept fell, with a single exception. The mysterious elder Galliard, Threefold Path, still resides in the area. He is highly reclusive, rarely appearing at moots or other gatherings and holding position with no sept. Much of his time is spent travelling up and down the eastern seaboard or through the depths of the Umbra, though he makes his home in the Delaware Valley. It is rumored that he will soon depart this world for good.<br /> <br /> Uktena: Dreamrunner, an elderly Theurge, is the Ritemaster of the Marshall Island Sept, and has lived in the Delaware Valley for over 50 years. He is the only Uktena in the region of Native American stock. However, the Uktena have bred with many oppressed and downtrodden peoples over the years, and have kin of many different ethnicities. There are a small number of African American Uktena spread throughout the Delaware Valley. It\u2019s a little known fact, but some Uktena have also chosen to breed into Jewish populations around the world. There are not many of them, but most of them in the United States call New York City, New Jersey and Philadelphia home. There used to be more of both groups in the area, but most of them were based out of the Fairmount Sept and the Blue Hole Sept, both of which no longer exist. Their kin are still around, however, so their populations may rebound, given time.<br /> <br /> Wendigo: The Wendigo control a single caern in the Delaware Valley, the Cohanzick Sept at the recently reclaimed Cohanzick Tribal Grounds in South Jersey. There are a small number of packs based there, and a small community of their kin among the Nanticoke Leni Lenape Tribal Nation that reclaimed the land. Prior to its destruction, the Fairmount Sept included at least three Wendigo members, but all three were killed when the Sept was destroyed in 1999. Their kin, largely descended from Native Americans that moved to Philadelphia in the mid-20<sup>th</sup> century as construction workers working on the city\u2019s skyscrapers (\u201cUrban Indians\u201d), still live in West Philly. At least one of their children has undergone First Change since the fall of Fairmount, and was accepted by the Wendigo of the Cohanzick Sept. There are also rumors that one of the new Canadian players on the Philadelphia Wings might be Wendigo kin; several of the Canadian players on the team are ethnically Iroquois, including the new owner.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <u>Some Noteworthy Caerns Outside the Immediate Area</u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u>Sept of the Boardwalk</u>- A Glass Walker dominated Level 3 caern of plenty at the Wyld West Casino in Atlantic City, NJ.<br /> <u>Trexler Sept</u>- A Glass Walker dominated Level 2 caern with some Bone Gnawer presence at Texler Memorial Park in Allentown, PA, named for Glass Walker ancestor Harry Clay Trexler.<br /> <u>Sept of the Hidden Peak</u>- A closed Red Talon controlled Level 1 Caern of Strength hidden in the Poconos, in the Appalachian Mountains of Pennsylvania.<br /> <u>Trenton Green Sept</u>- A mixed Bone Gnawer and Glass Walker Level 1 caern at Cadwalader Park in Trenton, NJ.<br /> <u>Long Pier Sept</u>- An open Get of Fenris controlled Level 1 caern on the waterfront of Cape May, NJ, near the Coast Guard Training Facility.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <u>Fera</u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Bastet: The Croatan were not the only shape-shifters to call the Delaware Valley home. The were-cougars were also native to this area. Their feline kin have been extirpated from the region, but rumors persist that some of the solitary werecats remain. During the war with the tainted Shadow Lords, one pack claimed to have been saved when a powerful werecougar came from nowhere to join them in battle, only to disappear soon after. Several packs reported seeing a similar figure during the final battle to reclaim the Caern of the Thundering Pines, but if he was there, he was nowhere to be found after the fight was done.<br /> <br /> Corax: There are known to be a few Corax native to Philadelphia. One works as a private investigator, the other as a reporter. They occasionally provide information to the Garou, but do not tend to mingle in our society overmuch. Perhaps we intimidate them?<br /> <br /> Gurahl: Are there Gurahl in the Delaware Valley? Well, there\u2019s a story going around about that. The Silver Fangs of the Sept of the New World\u2019s Glory claim that they found out about a Gurahl in the area. Knowing what renowned healers the Gurahl were, the Silver Fangs put aside their prejudice and went to this Gurahl, asking him to heal their comrades wounded in fighting the Wyrm. Instead, the Gurahl attacked them. As to whether the Gurahl was wyrm tainted, or simply still angry about the abuses his kind had suffered, the rumors disagree. What they do not disagree about is the result- the Silver Fang pack killed the Gurahl in self-defense. Are there more in the area? Well, on the one hand, the Gurahl the Silver Fangs killed had to come from somewhere. On the other hand, there aren\u2019t many Gurahl left in the world, and they\u2019re supposed to be pretty solitary. Who can say?<br /> <br /> Mokole: You\u2019re kidding, right? The whole \u201caligators in the sewer\u201d thing is in New York, not here.<br /> <br /> Ratkin: Like any other urban area, Philadelphia, Camden and the other cities of the Delaware Valley are known to harbor Ratkin. Encounters with them are rare, however, and their numbers are presumably few. After all, they suffered like every other Fera from the War of Rage, and if their numbers had recovered sufficiently to be a threat, the Garou would undoubtedly know of it. They are largely beneath notice.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <u>The Wyrm</u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Black Spiral Dancers: The fallen tribe has long had a significant presence in the Delaware Valley, much to the consternation of the Gaian garou. While their numbers were curtailed during the war, they were smart enough to effect a strategic withdrawal when it became obvious that their tainted Shadow Lord allies would fall. It is rumored that Delaware has become their stronghold, now that no Gaian caerns remain active there.<br /> <br /> Known Hives: Exact locations are difficult to pin down. The garou of Philadelphia have long believed that there is a hive buried somewhere under the city, but they have been unable to locate it despite decades of searching. There are believed to be at least two hives in Delaware and another in South Jersey, but their exact locations are harder to pin down. One small hive in the South Jersey city of Bridgeton was wiped out during the war, however.<br /> <br /> There are troublesome rumors and mutterings among the spirits about the Marcellus Shale in Pennsylvania. The environmental damage being caused by hydraulic fracking is already proving to be a boon for the creation of Banes. The possibility of the Black Spirals using the disruption to create a new, powerful Hive cannot be ignored, but so far no direct evidence of it has been found.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <u>Others</u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Vampires: There are a lot of vampires in Philadelphia and Camden. A whole lot. They\u2019re powerful, and they\u2019re dangerous. To make matters worse, they seem to travel in packs. Don\u2019t try to take them on alone, unless absolutely necessary. The local vampires seem to be organized along some twisted religion, with leaders calling themselves priests and bishops and such. The most powerful vampire in the area is, in fact, their Bishop and leader, a deformed monstrosity calling himself \u201cThe Warlord.\u201d Whatever his real name may be, he lives up to his moniker. A twelve foot tall behemoth of twisted flesh, he moves faster than something his size should be able to, is as strong as any garou and is attended by a small army of deformed minions, disgusting mockeries of life twisted into war machines. He has four arms, razor sharp teeth and claws and eyes as black as the abyss. He wears no clothes, since his skin is like the toughest armor, and to his back is strapped his greatest prize- Dawn\u2019s Pride, a Grand Klaive belonging to the Dawnstar family. The Warlord took it as a trophy when he slayed High Lord William Dawnstar\u2019s father, Edward. William tried to get it back, and lost an eye for his trouble (that\u2019s why they call him Dark Eye). All of William\u2019s garou children, and some of his grandchildren, died trying to get it back.<br /> <br /> Changelings: The Fae, or \u201cchangelings\u201d as they are sometimes called, have a strong presence in the Delaware Valley. They are believed to have a stronghold near the Marshall Island caern, and are said to have very good relations with the Garou of that sept, especially the Fianna (as might be expected). Beyond that, they mostly keep a low profile as far as the garou are concerned, but it is known that Independence Hall, where both the Declaration of Independence and the Constitution were written, is under their control. All cubs that spend any time in Philadelphia are warned of this, lest they inadvertently trespass where they shouldn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Mages: While there are undoubtedly human sorcerers in the Delaware Valley, they do not commonly have dealings with the Garou. Or, if they do, those dealings are not generally known. Some unexplained phenomena and happenings may be their doing, but the wise do not seek them out.<br /> <br /> Hunters: It has become obvious over the last 15 years that some new power has risen among the humans. Individuals with no obvious supernatural connection, who do not smell of Wyrm, Weaver or Wyld, have demonstrated impressive powers and a will to destroy anything non-human. Their powers are odd, but not overwhelming, their numbers are small, they do not seem to be organized and they tend to focus more on the vampires than they do on us. Most Garou try to avoid such creatures when they are encountered, as fighting them is rarely worth the trouble with so many other foes to face.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And there we have it. That should be enough to get started brainstorming character concepts. I look forward to hearing from any interested players. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":".  Changing Stargazer material 09-04-2014, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T23:35:05-07:00","id":244576,"title":"","content":"That is a <i>lot</i> of information! Well, as you know, I'm definitely up for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T23:42:52-07:00","id":244598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=244576#post244576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a <i>lot</i> of information! Well, as you know, I'm definitely up for it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. :-) I know we discussed some basics in PM, but please do me a favor and post what you're thinking about in terms of character concept here so other potential players can see.<br /> <br /> Just FYI everyone, I have another player as well, who is planning to play a Homid/Children of Gaia/Galliard. He needs to make an account on this forum first, though, so he'll homefully be around to post tomorrow.<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T00:44:50-07:00","id":244620,"title":"","content":"Alright, so as we've discussed, I'm planning to play a Homid/Children of Ga\u00efa/Philodox (Hopefully, he won't be redundant with the other CoG). He believes that one of the keys to Gaia's survival is through children's education, and so he wants to work as a youth educator, doing interventions in school to raise awareness about ecology, flora and fauna. I'd like him to be among the oldest of the pack, sort of a &quot;big bro&quot; figure, although I don't necessarily want to be the leader, if we have to elect one. I think he's gonna focus on social and physical stats, with Healing Gifts on the side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T07:40:14-07:00","id":244787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=244620#post244620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so as we've discussed, I'm planning to play a Homid/Children of Ga\u00efa/Philodox (Hopefully, he won't be redundant with the other CoG). He believes that one of the keys to Gaia's survival is through children's education, and so he wants to work as a youth educator, doing interventions in school to raise awareness about ecology, flora and fauna. I'd like him to be among the oldest of the pack, sort of a &quot;big bro&quot; figure, although I don't necessarily want to be the leader, if we have to elect one. I think he's gonna focus on social and physical stats, with Healing Gifts on the side.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not too worried about redundancy. The tribes themselves are very diverse, and allow for a wealth of character opportunities. Two player characters from the same tribe is not a problem at all, though (as I note above) I'd like to avoid more than two from the same tribe, if possible.<br /> <br /> As for leadership of the pack, that's something I plan to let happen IC. Every pack has a different dynamic and, as the group starts to RP together, I'm confident that will work itself out.<br /> <br /> So, how old were you thinking for the character? As I note above, I'm hoping for the majority of the characters to be in their mid-to-late teens (15-19), so a college-age character (18-19ish) would work just fine, assuming you're OK with him having gone through a relatively late First Change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T09:10:42-07:00","id":244837,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking 19. And yeah, I don't see any problem with a late First Change. Some people have a late puberty. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T09:15:10-07:00","id":244839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=244837#post244837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking 19. And yeah, I don't see any problem with a late First Change. Some people have a late puberty. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>OK. So, are you thinking a college student then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T09:32:38-07:00","id":244845,"title":"","content":"Yes, he's working on a degree in education, with a minor in natural science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T09:57:52-07:00","id":244855,"title":"","content":"Sounds good. Do you want your character (and his family) to be from the region, and attending a local college or university, or would you prefer him to be from away, with his family living elsewhere while he goes to college in the Delaware Valley?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T10:07:37-07:00","id":244858,"title":"","content":"Nah, local college or university it is. Otherwise, there wouldn't be any interaction with his family, and it wouldn't be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T12:53:28-07:00","id":244944,"title":"","content":"I'm the player mentioned above who is also interested. The only experience I have with the old World of Darkness is some VtM games, and they were a long time ago. I am more familiar with the new World of Darkness, but even then I spent more time playing Exalted than WoD. A lot of Werewolf is going to be new to me, and I don't know anything about the metaplot, so I'm looking to play a character who is as in the dark as I am.<br /> <br /> Named Scott, he's a Homid/Children of Gaia/Galliard. Scott grew up in a strange cult-like compound that belonged to the Silver Fangs. He left it when he moved to the big city for school, and has since become an LPN. Scott had his First Change after more than a few tragic probably-not-accidents, but had no desire to return to his family as they had expected. Instead he joined up with local Children of Gaia, and has since tried to absorb the culture. He's primarily a social character who loves peace and avoids violence when possible. While Scott espouses some of the Children of Gaia's ideology, at his core he just has a big heart and wants to help make his little corner of the world a better place. While nominally a pacifist, he contains inner rage for beings that deserve it so he can maintain an approachable image.<br /> <br /> He also hands with the Marshal Island Sept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T13:20:13-07:00","id":244954,"title":"","content":"Deathmatch &gt; Scott looks pretty interesting!<br /> <br /> Nutiket &gt; So, I've finally begun reading the W20 core book, and already I'm not that happy with my character concept. I think I'm going to rewrite it once I've finished reading the book, or at least when I'm far enough to have a cool idea in my head. I'm pretty sure my character will still be a Homid/Children of Gaia/Philodox though(although the Fianna are getting cooler every chapter...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T13:44:37-07:00","id":244978,"title":"","content":"The Marshal Island Sept is traditionally lead by the Fianna, so that could be a way for our characters to be friendly prior to the start of the game. They do have other Children of Gaia as well if you stick with that Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T21:41:31-07:00","id":245176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=244954#post244954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nutiket &gt; So, I've finally begun reading the W20 core book, and already I'm not that happy with my character concept. I think I'm going to rewrite it once I've finished reading the book, or at least when I'm far enough to have a cool idea in my head. I'm pretty sure my character will still be a Homid/Children of Gaia/Philodox though(although the Fianna are getting cooler every chapter...).</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand. Nothing wrong with that; we are still in the brainstorming phase. :-) Just let me know what you're thinking, and whether you have any questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm the player mentioned above who is also interested. The only experience I have with the old World of Darkness is some VtM games, and they were a long time ago. I am more familiar with the new World of Darkness, but even then I spent more time playing Exalted than WoD. A lot of Werewolf is going to be new to me, and I don't know anything about the metaplot, so I'm looking to play a character who is as in the dark as I am.<br /> <br /> Named Scott, he's a Homid/Children of Gaia/Galliard. Scott grew up in a strange cult-like compound that belonged to the Silver Fangs. He left it when he moved to the big city for school, and has since become an LPN. Scott had his First Change after more than a few tragic probably-not-accidents, but had no desire to return to his family as they had expected. Instead he joined up with local Children of Gaia, and has since tried to absorb the culture. He's primarily a social character who loves peace and avoids violence when possible. While Scott espouses some of the Children of Gaia's ideology, at his core he just has a big heart and wants to help make his little corner of the world a better place. While nominally a pacifist, he contains inner rage for beings that deserve it so he can maintain an approachable image.<br /> <br /> He also hands with the Marshal Island Sept. </div> </div> </div>Looking good. Of course, you and I have gotten into some pretty serious detail, so I don't have a lot I need to ask. :-) Are there any questions or concerns you have about the setting material, or any changes you want to make to the character concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T22:06:00-07:00","id":245188,"title":"","content":"I know that you said no to it, but I think that my character would really be better expressed as a vampiric were-cat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T22:06:51-07:00","id":245189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathmatchFM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=245188#post245188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that you said no to it, but I think that my character would really be better expressed as a vampiric were-cat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... let me think...<br /> <br /> No.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T22:10:36-07:00","id":245190,"title":"","content":"My next idea involves a Niwisha disguised as a Ragabash. <span style=\"color:#ffffff\">(I don't even know what this is)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T22:12:58-07:00","id":245191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathmatchFM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=245190#post245190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My next idea involves a Niwisha disguised as a Ragabash. <span style=\"color:#ffffff\">(I don't even know what this is)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Why did I invite you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T09:06:32-07:00","id":245371,"title":"","content":"Alright. I have a clearer idea for my character. I didn't really change the concept, but I tweaked it a bit, to make it more coherent.<br /> <br /> Geoff is still an Homid/Children of Gaia/Philodox. His parents are Kinfolk, but they didn't tell their two kids. However, they're aware of their nature because Geoff's uncle is Garou, but they never really envisioned that their own children would Change. His dad works at a charity organization he co-funded which offers <i>youth daycare and day camp</i>* during the holidays. Sometimes, he asks his sons to lend him a hand with the kids when they're short on staff. As such, Geoff spent his teenage years taking care of small kids, and while it didn't help his social life, he loved it, and wanted to become a teacher so he could help with their future. Of course, the First Change got in the way. The daycare center had recently received a stock of free toys generously offered by Avalon Plastic. And while the kids were happy at first, the Wyrm-taint in those toys was making them meaner and more capricious, and it also affected the staff, who was becoming increasingly bad-tempered.<br /> One day, when Geoff was alone with his dad at the center, cleaning up after the kids, they were attacked by a small team of Pentex employees, who was intent on abducting them so they could be corrupted by Banes, and ready to fully spread the Wyrm's influence on the center. But woe to them as Geoff experienced his First Change and fought back, killing some of them in the process. Fortunately, his dad had the presence of mind to call his Garou brother so that he could get there to calm his son before he accidentally kills him. They threw the toys away, and cut all ties from Avalon Plastic.<br /> <br /> Now a Garou, Geoff continues to work with the kids, but on a rarer basis. He has joined the Children of Gaia because he is convinced that educating the new generations, homid and garou, is essential to Gaia's survival. He has started working on a online degree in education with a minor in nature science, and he plans to do school interventions in the future, while in the meantime he sometimes visits his father's charity to teach the kids about fauna and flora. He is social and very open-minded, and wants nothing more than peace. However, he will show no mercy to those who harm children, and he has a hatred of big companies, as they could have made him into a Black Spiral Dancer.<br /> <br /> He also hangs out with the Marshall Island Sept. And there you go Deathmatch, now they know each other! x)<br /> <i>*=I'm not entirely sure this could exist in the US. It does here in France, and I tried to search for an equivalent, but I may be mistaken.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-31-2014, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T20:47:22-07:00","id":245836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=245371#post245371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright. I have a clearer idea for my character. I didn't really change the concept, but I tweaked it a bit, to make it more coherent.<br /> <br /> Geoff is still an Homid/Children of Gaia/Philodox. His parents are Kinfolk, but they didn't tell their two kids. However, they're aware of their nature because Geoff's uncle is Garou, but they never really envisioned that their own children would Change. His dad works at a charity organization he co-funded which offers <i>youth daycare and day camp</i>* during the holidays. Sometimes, he asks his sons to lend him a hand with the kids when they're short on staff. As such, Geoff spent his teenage years taking care of small kids, and while it didn't help his social life, he loved it, and wanted to become a teacher so he could help with their future. Of course, the First Change got in the way. The daycare center had recently received a stock of free toys generously offered by Avalon Plastic. And while the kids were happy at first, the Wyrm-taint in those toys was making them meaner and more capricious, and it also affected the staff, who was becoming increasingly bad-tempered.<br /> One day, when Geoff was alone with his dad at the center, cleaning up after the kids, they were attacked by a small team of Pentex employees, who was intent on abducting them so they could be corrupted by Banes, and ready to fully spread the Wyrm's influence on the center. But woe to them as Geoff experienced his First Change and fought back, killing some of them in the process. Fortunately, his dad had the presence of mind to call his Garou brother so that he could get there to calm his son before he accidentally kills him. They threw the toys away, and cut all ties from Avalon Plastic.<br /> <br /> Now a Garou, Geoff continues to work with the kids, but on a rarer basis. He has joined the Children of Gaia because he is convinced that educating the new generations, homid and garou, is essential to Gaia's survival. He has started working on a online degree in education with a minor in nature science, and he plans to do school interventions in the future, while in the meantime he sometimes visits his father's charity to teach the kids about fauna and flora. He is social and very open-minded, and wants nothing more than peace. However, he will show no mercy to those who harm children, and he has a hatred of big companies, as they could have made him into a Black Spiral Dancer.<br /> <br /> He also hangs out with the Marshall Island Sept. And there you go Deathmatch, now they know each other! x)<br /> <i>*=I'm not entirely sure this could exist in the US. It does here in France, and I tried to search for an equivalent, but I may be mistaken.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we have day-cares and such. No big deal there.<br /> <br /> When you say Geoff's uncle came to &quot;calm&quot; him... think more along the lines of &quot;forcibly restrain until the frenzy passes,&quot; unless the Uncle has a gift that allows him to pull someone out of frenzy.<br /> <br /> Now, if Uncle Bob (or whatever name we decide on) lives close enough to have arrived in the nick of time after Geoff's First Change, that means he's one of the local garou and belongs to one of the local septs. So, let's start with him. Tell me what you're thinking in terms of Uncle Bob.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T02:41:10-07:00","id":246041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=245836#post245836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you say Geoff's uncle came to &quot;calm&quot; him... think more along the lines of &quot;forcibly restrain until the frenzy passes,&quot; unless the Uncle has a gift that allows him to pull someone out of frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was implicit enough. ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=245836#post245836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if Uncle Bob (or whatever name we decide on) lives close enough to have arrived in the nick of time after Geoff's First Change, that means he's one of the local garou and belongs to one of the local septs. So, let's start with him. Tell me what you're thinking in terms of Uncle Bob.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uncle Steve, also known as Growl in The Wind, is an Ahroun of the Fianna, who is also a member of the Marshall Island Sept and has quite a Renown as a warrior. He however has a strained relationship with his brother Mark, who, despite being kin, can't stand the fact that Steve is essentially a murderer, even if it's for the &quot;good of the planet&quot;, and one that <i>enjoy</i> it.<br /> Steve doesn't really care about his brother's opinion, but he still loves his family, as he doesn't have one himself : no child of his own, and no wife. He had numerous girlfriends, but nothing that lasted. He's waiting for the perfect Kinfolk girl. So he spends most of his time with his pack, patrolling the area around the Marshall Island Sept. He likes his two nephews, even if he could only see them once every year for Christmas or Thanksgiving, and is delighted that one of them has become a Garou, as it means he get to spend more time with him. However, he's somewhat disappointed that Geoff decided to join the Children of Gaia and not the Fianna. He has decided to teach him how to fight like a true wolf, but laments at his pacifism. Still, he's supportive and keeps an eye on him. Maybe one day, he'll have a cub on his own that will properly follow on his footsteps, and will carry on his legacy and his breed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T08:32:09-07:00","id":246161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=246041#post246041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uncle Steve, also known as Growl in The Wind, is an Ahroun of the Fianna, who is also a member of the Marshall Island Sept and has quite a Renown as a warrior. He however has a strained relationship with his brother Mark, who, despite being kin, can't stand the fact that Steve is essentially a murderer, even if it's for the &quot;good of the planet&quot;, and one that <i>enjoy</i> it.<br /> Steve doesn't really care about his brother's opinion, but he still loves his family, as he doesn't have one himself : no child of his own, and no wife. He had numerous girlfriends, but nothing that lasted. He's waiting for the perfect Kinfolk girl. So he spends most of his time with his pack, patrolling the area around the Marshall Island Sept. He likes his two nephews, even if he could only see them once every year for Christmas or Thanksgiving, and is delighted that one of them has become a Garou, as it means he get to spend more time with him. However, he's somewhat disappointed that Geoff decided to join the Children of Gaia and not the Fianna. He has decided to teach him how to fight like a true wolf, but laments at his pacifism. Still, he's supportive and keeps an eye on him. Maybe one day, he'll have a cub on his own that will properly follow on his footsteps, and will carry on his legacy and his breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Steve the elder or younger brother?<br /> <br /> You are correct that young Garou can choose which Tribe they join, whatever their heritage may be. Kin, however, are the kin of whatever tribe they are descended from. So, are Geoff's parents Fianna kin, or Children of Gaia kin? Or is the father Fianna kin and the mother Children of Gaia kin? Or some other combination?<br /> <br /> And, while we're on the subject, what does Geoff's mother think of all this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T09:22:10-07:00","id":246188,"title":"","content":"Steve's the elder brother.<br /> <br /> Mark is also Fianna kin, and both brothers have some measure of pure blood. Although he doesn't care one bit.<br /> Geoff's mother, Allison, is a Children of Gaia kin, and two of them have met through their own Garou relatives : in her case it was her cousin. She's an children's book illustrator, who works at home, and sometimes helps her husband at the center. She's scared of what will happen to his son, but she's also immensely proud that he decided to join the Children of Gaia, and not some brutal tribe like the Get of Fenris. Or worse, those dirty Bone Gnawers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T09:28:13-07:00","id":246189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=246188#post246188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Steve's the elder brother.<br /> <br /> Mark is also Fianna kin, and both brothers have some measure of pure blood. Although he doesn't care one bit.<br /> Geoff's mother, Allison, is a Children of Gaia kin, and two of them have met through their own Garou relatives : in her case it was her cousin. She's an children's book illustrator, who works at home, and sometimes helps her husband at the center. She's scared of what will happen to his son, but she's also immensely proud that he decided to join the Children of Gaia, and not some brutal tribe like the Get of Fenris. Or worse, those dirty Bone Gnawers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure Breed is tribe specific, but since Allison is CoG kin, it's OK for Geoff to have some pure breed, as long as it is a low level. Not above 2, I'd say, unless the mom is ridiculously purely bred.<br /> <br /> Now, I believe you mentioned when we were talking before that Mark is the younger brother. High School age, or thereabouts?<br /> <br /> I know you don't know the area very well. Did you want the family to be in an urban area, or a suburban area, or a rural area? I can work with you on any of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T09:44:16-07:00","id":246194,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure yet if I'm going to take Pure Breed, we'll see if I have enough background points. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think you have the names mixed up : Mark is Geoff's father. I didn't name the kid's younger brother yet, but I'd call him Aaron. He's in junior year. While he likes his brother, he's somewhat jealous of him being the one to Change, especially since he learned about their family's lineage (&quot;I could have been so respected!&quot;). Also, if anyone asks him, he would have definitely chosen to become a Fianna.<br /> <br /> I'd like the Bolen family (there, I've finally named them all!) to live in a suburban area. However, Steve has chosen to live in a more rural place, to avoid hurting neighbors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T14:17:03-07:00","id":246361,"title":"","content":"This sounds like something I could be interested in.<br /> <br /> I've kind of always had this idea for a Silver Fang Ahroun. A teenage cheerleader, kind of valley girl, really cult of personality. Queen bee, really Rich, spoiled, and then bam, she goes through the first change and has to become a Werewolf. This sounds like one of the few games I'd ever get the play that character in. I'd have to brush up a bit on my W:tA, and read your setting material more in depth, but if that sounds like a cool concept to you let me know.<br /> <br /> -Cheers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T20:51:20-07:00","id":246604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=246194#post246194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure yet if I'm going to take Pure Breed, we'll see if I have enough background points. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think you have the names mixed up : Mark is Geoff's father. I didn't name the kid's younger brother yet, but I'd call him Aaron. He's in junior year. While he likes his brother, he's somewhat jealous of him being the one to Change, especially since he learned about their family's lineage (&quot;I could have been so respected!&quot;). Also, if anyone asks him, he would have definitely chosen to become a Fianna.<br /> <br /> I'd like the Bolen family (there, I've finally named them all!) to live in a suburban area. However, Steve has chosen to live in a more rural place, to avoid hurting neighbors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about the name mix-up. Anyway, plenty of suburban areas for the family to live in. I guess the first decision is whether you want them to live on the New Jersey side or the Pennsylvania side, and where you want them to fall on the income scale (lower middle class, middle class, upper middle class, upper class, etc.). I can help you narrow it down from there. As for Geoff, well, there are plenty of rural areas around the Marshal Island sept, particularly around Upper Bucks County, which is mostly more-or-less rural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrMarkers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=246361#post246361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like something I could be interested in.<br /> <br /> I've kind of always had this idea for a Silver Fang Ahroun. A teenage cheerleader, kind of valley girl, really cult of personality. Queen bee, really Rich, spoiled, and then bam, she goes through the first change and has to become a Werewolf. This sounds like one of the few games I'd ever get the play that character in. I'd have to brush up a bit on my W:tA, and read your setting material more in depth, but if that sounds like a cool concept to you let me know.<br /> <br /> -Cheers</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a very cool concept to me. You're more than welcome. So, for starters, did she know that she was from a kinfolk family, or was she totally in the dark about Garou prior to her first change? If she didn't know, did her parents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T23:40:50-07:00","id":246673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=246604#post246604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry about the name mix-up. Anyway, plenty of suburban areas for the family to live in. I guess the first decision is whether you want them to live on the New Jersey side or the Pennsylvania side, and where you want them to fall on the income scale (lower middle class, middle class, upper middle class, upper class, etc.). I can help you narrow it down from there. As for Geoff, well, there are plenty of rural areas around the Marshal Island sept, particularly around Upper Bucks County, which is mostly more-or-less rural.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have any good reason for that, but I'd say Pennsylvania. As for social income, lower middle class seems correct, considering the parents' jobs.<br /> And nope, you mixed the names again! Geoff is my character, and his Garou uncle is Steve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T12:15:55-07:00","id":247032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=246604#post246604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like a very cool concept to me. You're more than welcome. So, for starters, did she know that she was from a kinfolk family, or was she totally in the dark about Garou prior to her first change? If she didn't know, did her parents?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going with her parents knew, but kind of hopped she would never go through her first change, as she just wasn't Garou material in their eyes. Not that they dislike her or ever told her that, but just kind of, &quot;oh jeez&quot; after her first change. I'll also go with that they tried to introduce the idea to her, but she was kind of of like, &quot;omg mom and dad quit being such hippy weirdos.&quot; Like they were trying to prep her for it, but she was such an out of control teen they were too little too late.<br /> <br /> Now that she's post first change though and learning what it means to be a Silver Fang, she's kind of full of herself for it. She's always been an alpha, this makes sense to her.<br /> <br /> Part of the setting mentions -<br /> <br /> The caern is currently led by High Lord William Dark-Eye Dawnstar, an old Elder Ahroun who was a renowned warrior in his day. All of his Garou children and several grandchildren have died, however, leaving a single young garou grandchild who has yet to complete their rite of passage to be the heir apparent.<br /> <br /> I'm so willing to be that Grandchild<br /> <br /> Cheers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","user":"MrMarkers","date":". 09-02-2014, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T13:29:07-07:00","id":247100,"title":"","content":"What if she was going to the same high school than Geoff's brother? This could make a nice connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T14:31:54-07:00","id":247121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=247100#post247100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if she was going to the same high school than Geoff's brother? This could make a nice connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see no reason that this isn't possible, and I'm down with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T20:43:22-07:00","id":247408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=246673#post246673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have any good reason for that, but I'd say Pennsylvania. As for social income, lower middle class seems correct, considering the parents' jobs.<br /> And nope, you mixed the names again! Geoff is my character, and his Garou uncle is Steve.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, actually, I got it right that time. I assumed that Geoff was going to be basing himself somewhere near the Marshal Island Sept. On the other hand, if you intended for him to be based out of one of the other local septs, and just hang out at Marshal Island a lot because his Uncle is there, that's cool, too. What were you thinking?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrMarkers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=247032#post247032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going with her parents knew, but kind of hopped she would never go through her first change, as she just wasn't Garou material in their eyes. Not that they dislike her or ever told her that, but just kind of, &quot;oh jeez&quot; after her first change. I'll also go with that they tried to introduce the idea to her, but she was kind of of like, &quot;omg mom and dad quit being such hippy weirdos.&quot; Like they were trying to prep her for it, but she was such an out of control teen they were too little too late.<br /> <br /> Now that she's post first change though and learning what it means to be a Silver Fang, she's kind of full of herself for it. She's always been an alpha, this makes sense to her.<br /> <br /> Part of the setting mentions -<br /> <br /> The caern is currently led by High Lord William Dark-Eye Dawnstar, an old Elder Ahroun who was a renowned warrior in his day. All of his Garou children and several grandchildren have died, however, leaving a single young garou grandchild who has yet to complete their rite of passage to be the heir apparent.<br /> <br /> I'm so willing to be that Grandchild<br /> <br /> Cheers</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering if anyone was going to grab onto that hook. :-) If you're interested in playing Dark-Eye Dawnstar's grandchild, that would be just fine with me. Actually, your character concept is very similar to the NPC concept I was thinking about to fill the roll if no PC wanted to do it. Your character's last name would have to be Dawnstar, and she'd have to have a high pure breed even for a Silver Fang (preferably 5, but you could get away with 4), but those requirements aside your concept would work very well for the role. Just bear in mind that there will be a lot of expectations on the character, particularly from the other Silver Fangs in the setting. She'd have a lot to live up to if she wants to impress them. Also, the family line comes with a few built in enemies, particularly among the vampires of Philadelphia. Just makes for more fun story, though. :-) So, is that what you want to do?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=247100#post247100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if she was going to the same high school than Geoff's brother? This could make a nice connection.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrMarkers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=247121#post247121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see no reason that this isn't possible, and I'm down with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds good to me. Most of the Silver Fang kinfolk in the region live in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philadelphia_Main_Line\" target=\"_blank\">Main Line suburbs</a>, but there are other options available if that region doesn't suit what you have in mind for your characters' kinfolk families, Markers and Marmelade. Of course, if Geoff's brother and Markers' cheerleader are in the same high school, I assume that Geoff himself also went to that school, yes?<br /> <br /> Were you guys thinking a public, private or parochial school?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T22:53:45-07:00","id":247496,"title":"","content":"Ah, I get it. You're assuming that Geoff isn't living with his parents anymore. I'd say he doesn't have his own place yet, and still lives with them. Sometimes he crashes his uncle's couch when he's too tired to go back after a night of training, and sometimes he sleeps at the sept itself. The Bolen family isn't <i>that</i> far from the sept : I'd say twenty to thirty minutes by car from it. Ah, and Geoff has his driving license.<br /> But right now, no, he doesn't have his own place. In a few years maybe.<br /> <br /> As for school, sure, Geoff went to the same school too (likely public, maybe private, definitely not parochial) as his brother. It might have been difficult for him, considering his Garou nature and the fact that he didn't really hang out with any club or clique, rather preferring to work with the kids at the charity. That might have give him a reputation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T23:02:22-07:00","id":247500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=247496#post247496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I get it. You're assuming that Geoff isn't living with his parents anymore. I'd say he doesn't have his own place yet, and still lives with them. Sometimes he crashes his uncle's couch when he's too tired to go back after a night of training, and sometimes he sleeps at the sept itself. The Bolen family isn't <i>that</i> far from the sept : I'd say twenty to thirty minutes by car from it. Ah, and Geoff has his driving license.<br /> But right now, no, he doesn't have his own place. In a few years maybe.<br /> <br /> As for school, sure, Geoff went to the same school too (likely public, maybe private, definitely not parochial) as his brother. It might have been difficult for him, considering his Garou nature and the fact that he didn't really hang out with any club or clique, rather preferring to work with the kids at the charity. That might have give him a reputation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thank you for the clarification about his living situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T05:39:37-07:00","id":247760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=247408#post247408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was wondering if anyone was going to grab onto that hook. :-) If you're interested in playing Dark-Eye Dawnstar's grandchild, that would be just fine with me. Actually, your character concept is very similar to the NPC concept I was thinking about to fill the roll if no PC wanted to do it. Your character's last name would have to be Dawnstar, and she'd have to have a high pure breed even for a Silver Fang (preferably 5, but you could get away with 4), but those requirements aside your concept would work very well for the role. Just bear in mind that there will be a lot of expectations on the character, particularly from the other Silver Fangs in the setting. She'd have a lot to live up to if she wants to impress them. Also, the family line comes with a few built in enemies, particularly among the vampires of Philadelphia. Just makes for more fun story, though. :-) So, is that what you want to do?<br /> <br /> That sounds good to me. Most of the Silver Fang kinfolk in the region live in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philadelphia_Main_Line\" target=\"_blank\">Main Line suburbs</a>, but there are other options available if that region doesn't suit what you have in mind for your characters' kinfolk families, Markers and Marmelade. Of course, if Geoff's brother and Markers' cheerleader are in the same high school, I assume that Geoff himself also went to that school, yes?<br /> <br /> Were you guys thinking a public, private or parochial school?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more than happy to bite the plot hook and see where it drags me. Besides, having Vampire enemies is always a good way to start a career. My idea for an actually character sheet is pretty wide open, so I'm sure I can fit in Pure Breed 5.<br /> <br /> I'd assume is most of the kin live in Main Line, then the Dawnstar line would too. My character actually started off in private school. But was moved to a public school to start high school, because A) they thought that she wasn't going to go through her first change, and B) her mom and dad thought it might humble her a little if she got out of the &quot;Elite&quot; mentality. It of course backfired completely making her the &quot;New Rich Girl,&quot; on campus for her Freshman year, which lead into her being Queen Bitch in Sophomore year. She went through her first change the Summer before Junior year.<br /> <br /> I'm going with her original school being Baldwin School, then she Transferred to Conestoga High School. And of course she still lives with mom and dad.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T06:18:18-07:00","id":247782,"title":"","content":"I was considering some things while giving Scott a complete write up, about having two Children of Gaia in the pack, and I don't think it's a good idea. Well rather, I think we'd benefit more if all members of the pack were from different Tribes. That gives us more variety in Gifts, and also opens up more opportunities for roleplaying. I think from an in-game perspective it makes more sense too. The pack is supposed to be a bonding effort between various tribes, but if one tribe was overly represented, such as the Children of Gaia, that tribe could take more credit for the pack's success, or perhaps that the Children of Gaia's mindset would dominate pack decisions.<br /> <br /> Evilmarmelade, I know you mentioned originally that Geoff could be a Fianna. When I made Scott I was picking between Children of Gaia and Stargazers. What do you think about one of us changing tribes? While Children of Gaia is the better fit for Scott, it wouldn't be difficult for me to rework some things and go with Stargazers instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T08:14:41-07:00","id":247866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrMarkers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=247760#post247760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm more than happy to bite the plot hook and see where it drags me. Besides, having Vampire enemies is always a good way to start a career. My idea for an actually character sheet is pretty wide open, so I'm sure I can fit in Pure Breed 5.<br /> <br /> I'd assume is most of the kin live in Main Line, then the Dawnstar line would too. My character actually started off in private school. But was moved to a public school to start high school, because A) they thought that she wasn't going to go through her first change, and B) her mom and dad thought it might humble her a little if she got out of the &quot;Elite&quot; mentality. It of course backfired completely making her the &quot;New Rich Girl,&quot; on campus for her Freshman year, which lead into her being Queen Bitch in Sophomore year. She went through her first change the Summer before Junior year.<br /> <br /> I'm going with her original school being Baldwin School, then she Transferred to Conestoga High School. And of course she still lives with mom and dad.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>OK, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conestoga_High_School\" target=\"_blank\">Conestoga High School</a> covers <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tredyffrin_Township,_Chester_County,_Pennsylvania\" target=\"_blank\">Tredyffrin </a>and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Easttown_Township,_Chester_County,_Pennsylvania\" target=\"_blank\">Easttown</a>, so the characters would need to be from one of those areas. Does that also work for you, Marmelade?<br /> <br /> Now, Markers, the first chapter of the game (which will include the characters' rite of passage) will be set just after midnight on January 1, 2014. So, if your character went through her first change that summer, she would have had several months to train and prepare for her rite of passage, which is certainly appropriate. So, if she's in the middle of her Junior year, that would make her... 16?<br /> <br /> Interesting side note- teens in PA can get a learner's permit at age 16. After 6 months with the learner's permit, they may get a provisional driver's license, which allows them to drive unsupervised under <a href=\"http://www.dmv.org/pa-pennsylvania/teen-drivers.php#Pennsylvania-Provisional-License\" target=\"_blank\">various conditions a teenager would find obnoxious</a>. They may then get a permanent driver's license at 17 and a half, or 18 if they never completed a driver's ed course. Of course, that's for people who choose to follow the law, and care about such things as traffic tickets. Do queen bitch teen rich girls who can turn into 9-foot tall death monsters care about such things?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathmatchFM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=247782#post247782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was considering some things while giving Scott a complete write up, about having two Children of Gaia in the pack, and I don't think it's a good idea. Well rather, I think we'd benefit more if all members of the pack were from different Tribes. That gives us more variety in Gifts, and also opens up more opportunities for roleplaying. I think from an in-game perspective it makes more sense too. The pack is supposed to be a bonding effort between various tribes, but if one tribe was overly represented, such as the Children of Gaia, that tribe could take more credit for the pack's success, or perhaps that the Children of Gaia's mindset would dominate pack decisions.<br /> <br /> Evilmarmelade, I know you mentioned originally that Geoff could be a Fianna. When I made Scott I was picking between Children of Gaia and Stargazers. What do you think about one of us changing tribes? While Children of Gaia is the better fit for Scott, it wouldn't be difficult for me to rework some things and go with Stargazers instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deathmatch, Marmelade, I don't want either of you to feel compelled to change your tribe. There's nothing wrong with having two members of the same tribe. There is plenty of diversity within the culture of each tribe to allow for more than one unique character concept. As for the gifts, yes you would both be drawing from the same list, but there are still auspice gifts to provide variety. Additionally, there are enough different tribal gifts that neither of you would ever learn all of them unless you devoted all your XP to that and nothing else.<br /> <br /> You do have a point about the intended multi-tribal nature of the pack, Deathmatch, but I don't want that to force a player to choose a tribe that he doesn't want to play.<br /> <br /> I guess the point is that it's up to you guys. If you want to change Scott to a Stargazer, Deathmatch, you can, and I can work with you to accommodate with as few changes to your character concept as possible. Marmelade, if you'd rather Geoff be a Fianna than a Child of Gaia, I can work with you on that, too. Either of you is welcome to make a change, but I don't want either of you to feel like you <i>need</i> to make a change. I intend for this to be a long term chronicle, and one of the most important parts of ensuring that that will happen is making sure that everyone is playing a character that they are happy with and that they enjoy.<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T10:58:16-07:00","id":248015,"title":"","content":"I really don't have any opinion on these two town, so I'd say the Bolen's are from Easttown, only because it is harder to misspell than Tredyffrin.<br /> <br /> Mmh. I really like the Children of Gaia, so I'd rather not change. (And if I keep Geoff as he is while switching him to Fianna, he'll be very similar to another character of mine). Still, I'll give it some thought. I'll give you my answer tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T12:59:03-07:00","id":248107,"title":"","content":"I think Scott gravitated to the Children of Gaia because they have an outlook that makes him comfortable. He grew up in an out-of-state &quot;cult compound&quot;-like environment that included more than a few really macho guys, with the Silver Fang pack being composed of members of his large family. Scott never really fit into that mold though. He's not much for hunting and seems to lack a lot of aggression, with more of a caretaker mentality. Scott would prefer a peaceful solution to problems, despite the fact that he understand there are times for fighting. The Children of Gaia are also the sort of tribe to take in Garou from other tribes, and Scott would be drawn to them at least on an unconscious level simply because he wants to be a part of that nurturing environment, instead of the strange way he grew up.<br /> <br /> If I were to do Stargazers, I'd have to change some aspects to Scott. Currently, Scott is more of a social character. He fits as the &quot;heart&quot; of a group. Not the brains, brawn, or big personality type. This mindset is probably what is most similar to Geoff, rather than merely tribal identity. As a Stargazer, Scott would have to be a bit more of an intellectual than he currently is. In the setting, only a small number of the Stargazers remained after they left for Asia, with the promise that they would send any new Garou born to them to Asia as well. This wouldn't fit for Scott, since he is of Silver Fang lineage, not Stargazer. So what I think would be most likely is that an elder member of the Stargazers, who is respected by the local Garou Nation, intends on either departing for Asia, or even departing the material world for a part of the Umbra so deep he does not plan to return. He'd be the last member of his pack alive, perhaps over a century old, but does not want to deprive the Garou Nation of the bonds he's formed with various spirits, other shapechangers, or strange beings that he has come to understand. <br /> <br /> In this, he would introduce Scott to the Stargazers. While a lot of this seems to be a stretch on Scott's concept, one aspect of him is that he is a prospective author, and has quite an imagination. Instead of being brought into a community of Children of Gaia and Fianna as I had originally intended, he could instead go on spirit voyages and faerie adventures on what to him feels like a strange journey to enlightenment and out-of-this-world fiction. This can fit with Scott because he has a big heart that can help bridge gaps that might exist between the Garou Nation and potential non-Garou allies. He's not the sort to discriminate or feel superiority for being a werewolf. His teacher would be staying for this group ceremony, at which point he intends on departing forever. That would be a big source of anxiety for Scott, since his teacher is all he has left at this point, and adds apprehension over what his pack will look like. In this version, Scott would know things. Left a mysterious journal, or taught a lot of important lessons, or having memorized cryptic sayings or something. I considered that his Stargazer mentor would of been called the &quot;Faewalker&quot;, if he had perhaps visited the land of the fae.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the large post. It was as largely exploratory, but I want to know what everyone else thinks. Are Scott and Geoff's concepts/personalities different enough that we can have meaningful interaction without stepping on toes, or does the spiritual and mystic side add something better to the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T16:13:33-07:00","id":248217,"title":"","content":"Mmh, unfortunately, the current Geoff is indeed pretty similar to Scott. As you said, their mindset are similar enough, except that Geoff may be more eager to pick up weapons if a fight can bring peace. He's constently trying to bottle his anger, so he can release it on those who deserve it. And yeah, &quot;caretaker mentality&quot;, that's exactly it. In fact, the only major difference between the two of them is their Auspice, and I'm pretty sure we're gonna take the same CoG gifts (Mother's touch, right?).<br /> <br /> I still haven't found a concept for a Fianna alternative, but I'm certain that it would be really different from the current Geoff. Out of curiosity, would your Stargazer still be a Galliard?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T19:11:10-07:00","id":248373,"title":"","content":"Okay, I am new to this and a little confused, but I did talk with the ST a bit over PM and I have a rough concept for a character. He's a Glass Walker Ahroun and a young biker based in the Society Hill sept. Still thinking of a name and backstory though, and could use some help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T06:29:27-07:00","id":248779,"title":"","content":"Having thought more about Stargazer!Scott, I've realized that I'm going to have to adjust quite a bit. CoG!Scott is about kindness in a cruel world, and he struggles against depression and anger by seeking to surround himself with people he cares about. He voices the views on unity that the Children of Gaia have, but deep down wants people to get along because his inner rage scares him and because he wants to be loved. This wouldn't fit for Stargazer!Scott. Stargazers are all about eastern thought and would seek to remove the desire for that attachment. So I will need to think on themes more and decide where to go with him. <br /> <br /> As for Auspice, I still like Galliard but I'm not sure. I would like to represent one of each Auspice in our pack though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T08:29:05-07:00","id":248884,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that what you're talking about is the Stargazer ideal. Not all of them buy it 100% or live up to it. They all try, but finding the middle way is harder, and actually reaching it isn't something any Gazer wants to do, because then they would stop being a part of the Wheel of Ages. Stargazers are really complex, and I love them, but unless you have access to their Tribe Book they're kind of hard to get. You have to learn a whole fake religion inside a game about a fake religion. (I'm not calling out anyone's real faith, but the Werewolf versions are different than the real world equivalent, knowing about Buddhism is helpful, but it does not give you what the Stargazers actually believe.) Silver Fangs are kind of the same way.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Camilla, Deathmatch, everyone. Remember this game is taking place Pre Rite of Passage. Your characters understanding of the Tribes isn't even fully developed yet when we go game on. Having a strong mortal back story and an idea of where you want the character to go is going to help a lot more than getting down the nitty gritty of why your character is in a particular Tribe. So unless you were bread for your tribe (Silver Fang, Shadow Lord, sometimes Get or Furies), then don't sweat it too much and just make a bomb diggity backstory.<br /> <br /> -Cheers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T12:12:38-07:00","id":249056,"title":"","content":"Whoo boy, I missed a lot. This is what happens when I let them schedule me for a double shift. :-P<br /> <br /> Markers, you kind of hit the nail on the head there. Deathmatch, remember that the tribes aren't straight-jackets, and that no character ever fits a tribal identity perfectly. There's absolutely nothing wrong with a Stargazer that desires to be loved. Or, to look at it from another direction, perhaps he chooses the Stargazer tribe because he thinks that detachment will free him from pain, only to discover that he is happier with some attachments... like those of his pack.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that compassion is also an essential part of the philosophy of the Stargazers. They may not always express it the same way that the Children of Gaia do, but the root of that compassion is the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=248373#post248373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I am new to this and a little confused, but I did talk with the ST a bit over PM and I have a rough concept for a character. He's a Glass Walker Ahroun and a young biker based in the Society Hill sept. Still thinking of a name and backstory though, and could use some help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome, Camilla. :-) First off, I think you need to consider what kind of biker your character is. More specifically, whether or not he is an outlaw biker. You mentioned the Pagan's MC when we were speaking, who are quite strong in the Delaware Valley. They also have significant ties to organized crime.<br /> <br /> To be clear- I am not saying there is <i>anything</i> wrong with your character being a criminal; in fact, I think it would be quite interesting. I'm just saying that it's a pretty core part of the concept that you want to think about.<br /> <br /> Secondly, give some thoughts to the character's family background. Why did he choose to become a member of a biker gang (outlaw or not) in the first place? What was his home life like, growing up? Was he raised in that subculture? Or is he rebelling against his parents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T15:07:11-07:00","id":249192,"title":"","content":"Count me in as another person interested. ;D After talking it over with the ST, my basic concept is a Lupus/Red Talon/Theurge (or Ragabash) raised in captivity. She's originally from the Sept of the Hidden Peak, but inner conflict between her upbringing and the Talon's policy on humans led her to follow Sunset Howl to the Sept of the Thundering Pines.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if she would have had contact with the others yet - any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T18:18:32-07:00","id":249339,"title":"","content":"So I've re-tuned some parts of my character concept, and while it remains similar, I at least wanted to give a good summary so other players would have an idea of where I'm going with him.<br /> <br /> The character is Scott, a Homid/Stargazer/Galliard. He grew up in a large Silver Fang family heavily invested in breeding (and inbreeding) in what is a rather cult-like compound somewhere in southern Virginia. He never quite fit in, and was allowed to go to college out of state, in Pennsylvania, with hopes that he'd at least learn some skills to bring to his family. While there he learned more of the outside world and met a girl who he liked and got engaged to. But his not wanting to come home did not sit well with his family, who called in some favors with the local Silver Fangs to give him a bit of harassment in hopes that he'd go running back to his family. Somewhere along the line, his fiancee even died in what seemed like a tragic accident. Scott crumbled emotionally and sank to a low point after this, and shortly later had his First Change.<br /> <br /> He was scouted out by an elder Stargazer, the last of his tribe remaining on the east coast and the only survivor of his pack after a century of service to Gaia. He trained Scott during this time, despite the fact that Scott is still very emotional and attached to the material world, he still shows potential. Once Scott is a full member of the tribe and joins a pack, his mentor plans on journeying to a faraway part of the Umbra with no intention of returning (he's getting older and expects to achieve total spiritual enlightenment, die, or both). Scott is very attached to his mentor since he feels like he's the only one he has in the world now, and his leaving, as well as Scott knowing he'll have to be with a pack of strangers for the rest of his life, is a source of anxiety for him that he fights hard. Scott is very much a character who is looking to find himself, but can easily embody a mystic and mysterious aspect of the group as he strives to maintain connections between the pack and the non-Garou that his mentor established bonds and covenants with over the years. His main sources of strife involve trying to find his place in the world, both the material and spirit, as well as his conniving family that feels disrespected and wronged that he did not continue their long lineage.<br /> <br /> I hope that this time around, Scott's role is a bit more clearly distinct from Geoff's, and that he has a unique niche with the group.<br /> <br /> Edit: I think it would really benefit our group if we have one of each Auspice, and Scott's concept works as a Theurge as well if necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3789,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","user":"DeathmatchFM","date":". 09-04-2014, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T20:03:21-07:00","id":249404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stir of Echoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=249192#post249192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Count me in as another person interested. ;D After talking it over with the ST, my basic concept is a Lupus/Red Talon/Theurge (or Ragabash) raised in captivity. She's originally from the Sept of the Hidden Peak, but inner conflict between her upbringing and the Talon's policy on humans led her to follow Sunset Howl to the Sept of the Thundering Pines.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if she would have had contact with the others yet - any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most likely, she would be meeting the others for the first time when they come together for their rite of passage. None of the other characters, so far, have any direct ties to the Sept of the Thundering Pines. That's OK, though; plenty of opportunity for bonding while you guys are fighting for your lives. :-D<br /> <br /> I see that you're still conflicted between Theurge and Ragabash. Tell me, what draws you to each Auspice? Tell me something about your character that would make her feel like a Theurge to you, and something that would make her feel like a Ragabash to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathmatchFM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=249339#post249339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've re-tuned some parts of my character concept, and while it remains similar, I at least wanted to give a good summary so other players would have an idea of where I'm going with him.<br /> <br /> The character is Scott, a Homid/Stargazer/Galliard. He grew up in a large Silver Fang family heavily invested in breeding (and inbreeding) in what is a rather cult-like compound somewhere in southern Virginia. He never quite fit in, and was allowed to go to college out of state, in Pennsylvania, with hopes that he'd at least learn some skills to bring to his family. While there he learned more of the outside world and met a girl who he liked and got engaged to. But his not wanting to come home did not sit well with his family, who called in some favors with the local Silver Fangs to give him a bit of harassment in hopes that he'd go running back to his family. Somewhere along the line, his fiancee even died in what seemed like a tragic accident. Scott crumbled emotionally and sank to a low point after this, and shortly later had his First Change.<br /> <br /> He was scouted out by an elder Stargazer, the last of his tribe remaining on the east coast and the only survivor of his pack after a century of service to Gaia. He trained Scott during this time, despite the fact that Scott is still very emotional and attached to the material world, he still shows potential. Once Scott is a full member of the tribe and joins a pack, his mentor plans on journeying to a faraway part of the Umbra with no intention of returning (he's getting older and expects to achieve total spiritual enlightenment, die, or both). Scott is very attached to his mentor since he feels like he's the only one he has in the world now, and his leaving, as well as Scott knowing he'll have to be with a pack of strangers for the rest of his life, is a source of anxiety for him that he fights hard. Scott is very much a character who is looking to find himself, but can easily embody a mystic and mysterious aspect of the group as he strives to maintain connections between the pack and the non-Garou that his mentor established bonds and covenants with over the years. His main sources of strife involve trying to find his place in the world, both the material and spirit, as well as his conniving family that feels disrespected and wronged that he did not continue their long lineage.<br /> <br /> I hope that this time around, Scott's role is a bit more clearly distinct from Geoff's, and that he has a unique niche with the group.<br /> <br /> Edit: I think it would really benefit our group if we have one of each Auspice, and Scott's concept works as a Theurge as well if necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Scott is still the only Galliard, and I think he works better that way anyway. I very much like the revised concept. I'm going to tweak the setting information to account for the new mentor character; he will be named &quot;Threefold Path.&quot; Do you still want Scott to be based out of the Marshall Island Sept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T00:06:35-07:00","id":249597,"title":"","content":"Geoff could work as a Galliard, if you wanna switch Scott to Theurge. Of course, it seems like I'm the only one who also envisions his character as a Philodox, so I'm not going to change unless you want another auspice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T06:49:09-07:00","id":249748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=249597#post249597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geoff could work as a Galliard, if you wanna switch Scott to Theurge. Of course, it seems like I'm the only one who also envisions his character as a Philodox, so I'm not going to change unless you want another auspice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Geoff works best as a Philodox, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T07:01:27-07:00","id":249754,"title":"","content":"Yeah, as he's written right now, I agree with you. But I could tweak it just a little bit if needed to make him more like a Galliard.<br /> <br /> As I said, won't do that for now, as nobody else wanna be a Philodox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T17:38:12-07:00","id":250245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=249404#post249404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that you're still conflicted between Theurge and Ragabash. Tell me, what draws you to each Auspice? Tell me something about your character that would make her feel like a Theurge to you, and something that would make her feel like a Ragabash to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>After mulling over it, I believe she works best as a Theurge. Her stealth and innate curiosity made me interested in Ragabash, but I think that, combined with her strong spirituality and nurturing personality made Theurge more fitting. I'd still be happy to play her as a Ragabash, though.<br /> <br /> ^^ Thought it might be helpful to make a census of what we have so far:<br /> <br /> <b>Breeds</b><br /> Homid: 4<br /> Metis: 0<br /> Lupus: 1<br /> <br /> <b>Auspices</b><br /> Ahroun: 2<br /> Galliard: 1<br /> Philodox: 1<br /> Theurge: 1<br /> Ragabash: 0<br /> <br /> <b>Tribes</b><br /> Children of Gaia: 1<br /> Glass Walkers: 1<br /> Red Talons: 1<br /> Silver Fangs: 1<br /> Stargazers: 1","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T17:43:08-07:00","id":250250,"title":"","content":"That's just fine. :-) So, tell me about her first change. I believe you said when we were talking via PM that the Talons came and got her before the change happened. So, when and how did it occur?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T22:31:34-07:00","id":250526,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how much time the Talons give their cubs before sending them off on their Rite of Passage, but I'd say she was taken from anywhere between 3 to 6 months ago. They weren't actually seeking her out, not at first - they had been planning to &quot;liberate&quot; the wolves of her sanctuary for some time. When they came, they &quot;culled&quot; what she considered to be her human pack, and whisked her and the other wolves off to their Sept.<br /> <br /> She was isolated from the others (in reality, under careful watch by their Thuerges), and in the week leading up to her Change she was ridden with dreams, thoughts, and hallucinations (visions?) no sane wolf should have. When the Change happened, they were there to guide her, and were all too eager to fill her head with their propaganda.<br /> <br /> As for the how, besides the whole liberation angle, I like the idea of a wayward Kin-Fetch letting them know of her existence. She could be descended from the purest Red Talons, but years back, one of her ancestors was captured by humans, and that wolf's descendent's have been passed around various zoo's, research facilities, and sanctuaries ever since. Her blood, while diluted, is pure - she's somebody's family - and that could be the catalyst that pushed the Talon's into action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T09:29:22-07:00","id":250811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stir of Echoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=250526#post250526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how much time the Talons give their cubs before sending them off on their Rite of Passage, but I'd say she was taken from anywhere between 3 to 6 months ago. They weren't actually seeking her out, not at first - they had been planning to &quot;liberate&quot; the wolves of her sanctuary for some time. When they came, they &quot;culled&quot; what she considered to be her human pack, and whisked her and the other wolves off to their Sept.<br /> <br /> She was isolated from the others (in reality, under careful watch by their Thuerges), and in the week leading up to her Change she was ridden with dreams, thoughts, and hallucinations (visions?) no sane wolf should have. When the Change happened, they were there to guide her, and were all too eager to fill her head with their propaganda.<br /> <br /> As for the how, besides the whole liberation angle, I like the idea of a wayward Kin-Fetch letting them know of her existence. She could be descended from the purest Red Talons, but years back, one of her ancestors was captured by humans, and that wolf's descendent's have been passed around various zoo's, research facilities, and sanctuaries ever since. Her blood, while diluted, is pure - she's somebody's family - and that could be the catalyst that pushed the Talon's into action.</div> </div> </div> </div>The length of time depends largely on how much time the cub needs to prepare, and varies greatly. 3-6 months is certainly fine.<br /> <br /> So, after a disaster of this nature, did the wolf sanctuary shut down? Or are they trying to rebuild?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T10:13:14-07:00","id":250860,"title":"","content":"Works been hectic this week, I should have a back story written up pretty soon, and I'm going to make a proto-character sheet when I do it. Based on the W:tA books fluff, I should probably just make the sheet without a Tribal Gift, unless you have other restrictions Jim.<br /> <br /> For my first change I'm going with it being after a party, and my character (tentatively now named Hannah Dawnstar), was drunk and driving, they got into an accident. Instead of just dying, her brain decided it would be a good idea for her to have her first change. Her Kin Fetch was like, omg better go get the Fangs, but by the time they showed up, she'd already killed and eaten the responding police officers, destroyed both cars, and killed a class mate. Without much left to destroy, and still weak from the car accident and being shot by the cops, the Fangs put her down easily.<br /> <br /> If it's cool with Geoff I'd have liked his little brother to be one of the kids in the car, I think that could be pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Another thing I was tossing around mentally is that her father is essentially barren, which is why she's an only child. However, in true Silver Fang fashion, her mother (the one with Dawnstar blood), has been being bred to various Fangs, as part of the duty to the family. After is resulted in her actually getting pregnant, and putting a rift her her relationship with her husband, she started to refuse. This has created a lot of tension with the family, and they kind of just wanted a normal life, which is made all the worse by Hannah actually going through her first change, dragging them all back into it. In truth Hannah's mother doesn't even know which Fang is Hannah's father. I'm guessing some of them do though. Of course Hannah is oblivious to all of this unless someone tells her, but she is aware that mom and dad have been struggling with their relationship, and weary of the family for awhile prior to her change.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking it would be cool if I could work into the sheet that I have a special connection to Isaiah Morningkill, as a spirit mentor. While it would be a big deal in the Fangs, Hannah doesn't know that, or really who he is. So whoever her dad is related to the Morningkill line. This might be a bit much though, as it would give her a legitimate tie to actually being somewhere in succession for the Silver Crown. I just like the idea of her main source of Wisdom in trouble being the ghost of a no nonsense Cowboy, who ultimately knows the darkest sides of the Fangs.<br /> <br /> -Cheers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T10:38:15-07:00","id":250881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrMarkers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=250860#post250860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Works been hectic this week, I should have a back story written up pretty soon, and I'm going to make a proto-character sheet when I do it. Based on the W:tA books fluff, I should probably just make the sheet without a Tribal Gift, unless you have other restrictions Jim.<br /> <br /> For my first change I'm going with it being after a party, and my character (tentatively now named Hannah Dawnstar), was drunk and driving, they got into an accident. Instead of just dying, her brain decided it would be a good idea for her to have her first change. Her Kin Fetch was like, omg better go get the Fangs, but by the time they showed up, she'd already killed and eaten the responding police officers, destroyed both cars, and killed a class mate. Without much left to destroy, and still weak from the car accident and being shot by the cops, the Fangs put her down easily.<br /> <br /> If it's cool with Geoff I'd have liked his little brother to be one of the kids in the car, I think that could be pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Another thing I was tossing around mentally is that her father is essentially barren, which is why she's an only child. However, in true Silver Fang fashion, her mother (the one with Dawnstar blood), has been being bred to various Fangs, as part of the duty to the family. After is resulted in her actually getting pregnant, and putting a rift her her relationship with her husband, she started to refuse. This has created a lot of tension with the family, and they kind of just wanted a normal life, which is made all the worse by Hannah actually going through her first change, dragging them all back into it. In truth Hannah's mother doesn't even know which Fang is Hannah's father. I'm guessing some of them do though. Of course Hannah is oblivious to all of this unless someone tells her, but she is aware that mom and dad have been struggling with their relationship, and weary of the family for awhile prior to her change.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking it would be cool if I could work into the sheet that I have a special connection to Isaiah Morningkill, as a spirit mentor. While it would be a big deal in the Fangs, Hannah doesn't know that, or really who he is. So whoever her dad is related to the Morningkill line. This might be a bit much though, as it would give her a legitimate tie to actually being somewhere in succession for the Silver Crown. I just like the idea of her main source of Wisdom in trouble being the ghost of a no nonsense Cowboy, who ultimately knows the darkest sides of the Fangs.<br /> <br /> -Cheers</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't write up a character sheet yet. I have some house rules that need to be considered, and I want to wait until we have everyone's back stories worked out first before we start doing stats.<br /> <br /> She <i>ate</i> the cops? Whoa. That's pretty ominous for a First Change. Killing is one thing, but cannibalism usually only happens when in the Thrall of the Wyrm (which happens when a frenzy is especially bad).<br /> <br /> Being in the car when that happens would have been a pretty traumatic experience for Geoff's brother, especially considering that he wasn't even present at Geoff's First Change. That's entirely up to you, Marmelade.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with that backstory for Hannah's birth. Just to be clear- was her mother sleeping with Silver Fangs because she was ordered to do so by her father (or other family members), or because she was trying on her own to do her &quot;duty&quot; as a kin by bearing children, or because she was dissatisfied with her husband, or because the Silver Fangs that wanted to breed with her were forcing her? I'm fine with any of these (or even a combination), but I need to know so I can decide how that story progresses and what the relationships are.<br /> <br /> The Morningkill connection is fine; the Dawnstars have bred with the Morningkill line before, so no issue there. Just make sure you take the Ancestors background, and I'd suggest the Ancestor Ally merit as well, to represent it mechanically, when the time comes to make the character sheets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T10:57:09-07:00","id":250908,"title":"","content":"Alright, no sheet yet.<br /> <br /> Yes, she ate the cops. The Fangs cleaned it up, but I wanted Geoff's brother to be there so someone outside of the Silver Fangs knows. It's kind of a sticking point for a lot of Fangs who already judge her as &quot;Dawnstar's little man eater.&quot; Up until her first change she was out of control, and a big part of the reform she's going through is realizing just how true that is. She <i>ate</i> people. If that isn't sobering, not much is.<br /> <br /> While Hannah is spoiled, and a bitch, she is trying to live up to being a Fang. She's trying to channel that into being a more humble Warrior of Gaia. It's a struggle that will define her as a character.<br /> <br /> As for Hannah's mother. mostly a mix of of father making her, and her wanting to preform the duty to the Tribe. She loves her husband, and wants to make that relationship work. If they weren't kinfolk, they'd have a good normal relationship. She's an accountant, he's a lawyer (IE: team Silver Fang, money managers). Things would be great for them. While they understand that their roles are necessary for the survival of Gaia, they also know that if they could turn a blind eye to it, and just live their lives they would be happier.<br /> <br /> I'll keep that in mind with Isiah Morningkill, and write it into the back ground. A big part of why Hannah is the way she is was this fascination she had with the wild west mentality growing up. She had visions of cowboys and just being a badass, of settling things with cutting words and fist fights. She kind of grew out of it as she got older, but she remembers the old Grey Haired cowboy always in her dreams.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","user":"MrMarkers","date":". 09-06-2014, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T11:02:17-07:00","id":250911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrMarkers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=250908#post250908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, no sheet yet.<br /> <br /> Yes, she ate the cops. The Fangs cleaned it up, but I wanted Geoff's brother to be there so someone outside of the Silver Fangs knows. It's kind of a sticking point for a lot of Fangs who already judge her as &quot;Dawnstar's little man eater.&quot; Up until her first change she was out of control, and a big part of the reform she's going through is realizing just how true that is. She <i>ate</i> people. If that isn't sobering, now much is.<br /> <br /> While Hannah is spoiled, and a bitch, she is trying to live up to being a Fang. She's trying to channel that into being a more humble Warrior of Gaia. It's a struggle that will define her as a character.<br /> <br /> As for Hannah's mother. mostly a mix of of father making her, and her wanting to preform the duty to the Tribe. She loves her husband, and wants to make that relationship work. If they weren't kinfolk, they'd have a good normal relationship. She's an accountant, he's a lawyer (IE: team Silver Fang, money managers). Things would be great for them. While they understand that their roles are necessary for the survival of Gaia, they also know that if they could turn a blind eye to it, and just live their lives they would be happier.<br /> <br /> I'll keep that in mind with Isiah Morningkill, and write it into the back ground. A big part of why Hannah is the way she is was this fascination she had with the wild west mentality growing up. She had visions of cowboys and just being a badass, of settling things with cutting words and fist fights. She kind of grew out of it as she got older, but she remembers the old Grey Haired cowboy always in her dreams.<br /> <br /> Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds great to me.<br /> <br /> As for Geoff's brother, as I said that's up to Marmelade since it's such a significant thing for that NPC. However, even if Geoff's brother wasn't there, I'm willing to have another kinfolk NPC from another tribe in the car, to suit your needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T11:09:43-07:00","id":250914,"title":"","content":"As you can see I've tried to dump a ton of Drama into the character, and a lot of flavor. She's not some Shining Fang Knight, but the interesting part about her is she <i>could</i> be. Which to me is way cool. Yeah, if Geoff's not cool with his brother being there, someone else who knows would be fine. I can already see that all my points are going into merits and backgrounds, which is cool I guess considering I'm shaping up to be the least adept at being a Garou of the gate is seems, which I'm cool with.<br /> <br /> Cheers<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T15:27:52-07:00","id":251090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=250811#post250811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The length of time depends largely on how much time the cub needs to prepare, and varies greatly. 3-6 months is certainly fine.<br /> <br /> So, after a disaster of this nature, did the wolf sanctuary shut down? Or are they trying to rebuild?</div> </div> </div> </div>The sanctuary's been shut down, and is now likely under investigation by the local/state government. The idea was to inspire fear and respect, but that backfired. People are definitely afraid, but there's no respect there. They're just afraid that a bunch of rabid wolves are on the loose. In the long term, that's probably going to have a negative effect on their wolf kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T17:47:53-07:00","id":251168,"title":"","content":"I'm always eager for more drama, so yes, Geoff's brother was in this damned car. Luckily for the others, as he was kinfolk, he wasn't affected for the delirium and managed to get most of the other kids out of the car to safety, maybe when Hannah was too busy eating the cops who had surely been firing shots at her.<br /> Indeed, it has been very traumatic, and while he was jealous of his brother, he is also very, <i>very</i> scared of him.<br /> <br /> Although, if Hannah's had eaten a kid, I'm pretty sure that Geoff's brother isn't jealous anymore, but just plain hostile and hateful to Garous. It might be a little extreme, and it would profundly change his character at the core. So...yes to being in the car and witnessing the death of the cops, but no to the murder of a classmate. Maybe she could have mauled the kid, without downright killing him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 09-07-2014, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T08:00:27-07:00","id":251474,"title":"","content":"I'm down with just backhanding one hard enough to break an arm or something. It can be just the cops that took the full brunt of the assault, which I think makes sense. They probably know where kids like to party so they were pretty damn quick to being on the scene, probably driving past the accident within minutes of it happening. So after the crash itself, and Hannah having to jaws of life herself out of the car in Chrinos, she only managed to backhand one of the other kids away while Geoff's brother was trying to get them to cooperate. The cops rolled up and watched a monster backhand a kid, and they went into hero fear delierium and fired shots, this drew her attention while the kids got away.<br /> <br /> -Cheers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","user":"MrMarkers","date":". 09-07-2014, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T19:08:20-07:00","id":251821,"title":"","content":"OK, I guess that settles the details with the car incident and Hannah's first change, then. I feel like, by now, we have a pretty good handle on Geoff, Hannah and Scott. I think everything else is ironing out details.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stir of Echoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=251090#post251090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The sanctuary's been shut down, and is now likely under investigation by the local/state government. The idea was to inspire fear and respect, but that backfired. People are definitely afraid, but there's no respect there. They're just afraid that a bunch of rabid wolves are on the loose. In the long term, that's probably going to have a negative effect on their wolf kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, not usually a good thing for the local wolf population. And that's certainly not going to endear the other local septs to the Hidden Peak Sept (not that they needed any more reasons). So, how does Stir of Echoes feel about the prospect of joining up with a pack of werewolves, now that the time has come for her rite of passage (especially given what happened to her old wolf pack and human &quot;pack&quot;)? Is she eager to be with a new social unit? Curious about the new people she'll meet? Apprehensive about being thrust into a new situation? Worried about the challenges of her Rite of Passage? I ask because I'm trying to get a feel (and help you get a feel) for how Stir of Echoes will be dealing with some of the new situations she will be exposed to. Character backstory for a Lupus is often harder than for the other two breeds, since their pre-change lives are both much shorter and much harder for us as humans to relate to. So, with Lupus, it's often more about getting a feel for what the character is like than for determining a large number of specific events and individuals in the backstory, as we do for the Homid characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=248373#post248373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I am new to this and a little confused, but I did talk with the ST a bit over PM and I have a rough concept for a character. He's a Glass Walker Ahroun and a young biker based in the Society Hill sept. Still thinking of a name and backstory though, and could use some help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, Camilla, haven't heard much from you since you first posted. How's the character concept coming along? If you'd like, why not post what ideas you have, and we can help you brainstorm? As you can see, we seem to have a pretty good synergy going on here. :-)<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T16:49:47-07:00","id":252768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=251821#post251821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, not usually a good thing for the local wolf population. And that's certainly not going to endear the other local septs to the Hidden Peak Sept (not that they needed any more reasons). So, how does Stir of Echoes feel about the prospect of joining up with a pack of werewolves, now that the time has come for her rite of passage (especially given what happened to her old wolf pack and human &quot;pack&quot;)? Is she eager to be with a new social unit? Curious about the new people she'll meet? Apprehensive about being thrust into a new situation? Worried about the challenges of her Rite of Passage? I ask because I'm trying to get a feel (and help you get a feel) for how Stir of Echoes will be dealing with some of the new situations she will be exposed to. Character backstory for a Lupus is often harder than for the other two breeds, since their pre-change lives are both much shorter and much harder for us as humans to relate to. So, with Lupus, it's often more about getting a feel for what the character is like than for determining a large number of specific events and individuals in the backstory, as we do for the Homid characters.<br /> <br /> -Jim</div> </div> </div> </div>She's a bit overwhelmed with everything right now. She's definitely eager to be with a new pack, as to have a pack is to have a family that (in her view) would bring a much desired stability to her life. At the same time, she's afraid. There's so many things to take in, to learn and to accomplish. She struggles to keep balance between her wolf, human, and spirit halves. She worries that if she can't keep up with what's expected of her, her pack might be taken away again - or worse, be torn apart by her own failures. Echo's a character plagued by self-doubt, torn between her Tribe's doctrine and her own life's experience. Her mind's a mess.<br /> <br /> On the outside, she tries to hide all of this behind a blank face (not that she's any good at it. It tends to be blatantly obvious what she thinks and feels.). She'd never want to burden the pack with her personal baggage - the pack's problems always come before her own. This builds up to a lot of stress over time, which is just one more thing she'll have to deal with.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, she's quiet, preferring to observe and think things through over jumping headfirst into problems.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T17:00:20-07:00","id":252780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stir of Echoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=252768#post252768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's a bit overwhelmed with everything right now. She's definitely eager to be with a new pack, as to have a pack is to have a family that (in her view) would bring a much desired stability to her life. At the same time, she's afraid. There's so many things to take in, to learn and to accomplish. She struggles to keep balance between her wolf, human, and spirit halves. She worries that if she can't keep up with what's expected of her, her pack might be taken away again - or worse, be torn apart by her own failures. Echo's a character plagued by self-doubt, torn between her Tribe's doctrine and her own life's experience. Her mind's a mess.<br /> <br /> On the outside, she tries to hide all of this behind a blank face (not that she's any good at it. It tends to be blatantly obvious what she thinks and feels.). She'd never want to burden the pack with her personal baggage - the pack's problems always come before her own. This builds up to a lot of stress over time, which is just one more thing she'll have to deal with.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, she's quiet, preferring to observe and think things through over jumping headfirst into problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember, blatantly obvious to a wolf, lupus or more experienced Garou is not necessarily going to be blatantly obvious to a younger Homid character (like, say, our other 4 PCs). Homids are not always going to be automatically sensitive to the visual and olfactory clues that would express all of Stir of Echoes' emotions while in Lupus form. Just something to keep in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T17:25:00-07:00","id":252792,"title":"","content":"I will definitely keep that in mind. Figuring out the personality of a wolf given sapience has turned out to be a lot more difficult than I first imagined. ^-^&quot;<br /> <br /> Were there any other problems you noticed? Anything else I could write up to help define the character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T20:05:50-07:00","id":252906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=251821#post251821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, Camilla, haven't heard much from you since you first posted. How's the character concept coming along? If you'd like, why not post what ideas you have, and we can help you brainstorm? As you can see, we seem to have a pretty good synergy going on here. :-)<br /> <br /> -Jim</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, a lot of stuff has happened to me in real-life, and I haven't had much time to do much. Been out of town for a few days and I practically forgot about this game. I am sorry about that. I'll try to get back on my character concept as best I can though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T16:50:31-07:00","id":254811,"title":"","content":"OK, well, I was hoping that giving Camilla a few days would help, but I guess you still need more time. I was planning to do this next step with everybody together, but instead I'll do it with everyone else while Camilla continues to brainstorm ideas.<br /> <br /> Over the course of the next day or two, I'll be sending all of you a private message. Essentially, it will be a personalized version of the general knowledge post, containing information about the setting that you can consider to be in character knowledge. As with the setting information post, each of you can consider this to be in character knowledge for your character. Once again, this knowledge will not always be accurate, and it will not always be complete. Whether your characters believe this information, in whole or in part, is up to you, but it is information that they have available to them.<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T18:54:16-07:00","id":254923,"title":"","content":"Sounds good Jim!<br /> <br /> I want to thank you for just how much passion and forethought you're putting into this, I can tell it's going to be great.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Markers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T09:51:03-07:00","id":256110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrMarkers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=254923#post254923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds good Jim!<br /> <br /> I want to thank you for just how much passion and forethought you're putting into this, I can tell it's going to be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur! I can't wait!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T06:33:29-07:00","id":257238,"title":"","content":"Excuse me, are you still recruiting for this game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T08:53:54-07:00","id":258189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=257238#post257238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excuse me, are you still recruiting for this game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, we're definitely still recruiting. We're primarily looking for a Ragabash character, but any interesting and fun concepts are welcome. What kind of character did you have in mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T06:35:14-07:00","id":258941,"title":"","content":"Oh, awesome, I actually wanted to play a Ragabash character! I can write out a little biography if that helps, apologies if you weren't looking for that:<br /> <br /> Narasimha-Vallabha (Or Val as he prefers to be called) was born in New York to an eccentric named Natasha Narula, a screenwriting lecturer at New York University. His father died of heart complications when he was only seven, so he was left to his mother's rather lax child-rearing methods, which consisted of letting him do whatever the hell he liked. Always interested in his Indian heritage, Val studied the Vedas as well as Sanskrit, and can rattle off shlokas with surprising ease. Sometimes they're even accurate.<br /> <br /> Just before entering university, his mother received a letter inviting her and her son to a reunion at the Narula clan's estate in Utter Pradesh. Natasha had no interest in going, but she was unusually insistent that her son attend. Ever-eager for new experiences, Val agreed.<br /> <br /> He arrived in a country unlike anything he'd imagined. No amount of Bollywood had prepared him for how different life in Hindustan was. Reaching his family's serene <i>hawaili</i> was something of a relief, and his relatives were infinitely gracious despite his awful Hindi. They arranged a magnificent dinner in his honor, and were positively obsequious. Rather an ostentatious affair for the prodigal son of the family's black sheep. In fact, everything was a bit suspicious...No one would stop smiling. And then there was this damn ringing in his ears, and then...<br /> <br /> He awoke to darkness, and an unholy thirst. A gentle, bearded face appeared at his side and offered him a glass of...something. Val drank it without thinking and returned to oblivion.<br /> <br /> Val discovered the gravity of his predicament when next he woke. He'd been left at the bottom of a deep, dry well. During the day, the well was sealed, but at night, he could gaze up at the magnificent star-studded heavens, and the moon, brighter then he'd ever seen it. His only companion was the bearded man, who appeared when he awoke, and offered him his only sustenance, something he called 'soma'.<br /> <br /> And Val dreamt, of days past, of gods and heroes, and wolves, always wolves. Moons slipped by alongside time, until existence itself seemed so little and insignificant. On a night of perfect, unbroken darkness, he stared into a beautiful abyss, and was filled with the very essence of life. Howling out in ecstasy, Val knew nothing but the rush of blood in his veins, and the frantic beat of his heart. Claws tore at stone walls, terrible teeth gnashed, and Val wanted to kill...And the bearded man appeared again, and Val flexed his talons, hungry for blood, but then the bearded man became something...<i>more</i>.<br /> <br /> Val entered a hidden world, he was one of the Chosen, or so he was told. The bearded man, named Dehazku, instructed him in the ancient arts of his tribe, stripping Val of his old name, his very identity, and preparing him for a life dedicated to his new family, Dehazku called them the 'Vrikodara Jata'. Dehazku, following some arcane series of astrological predictions had determined Val would be born with the mark of the moon, and was destined for great things. With manic eyes, Dehazku told Val told he was pure and fit for breeding, that he would lead his tribe to a new golden age, that he would help retake Hindustan from blood-drinking vetala and wicked demons who took the form of tigers. Quickly determining that Dehazku was slightly nuts, Val thought only of escape, and his poor mother, who'd given birth to a monster.<br /> <br /> So he fled, making for New York, but Val is deeply worried that Dehazku simply let him go, as a sort of test, it'd all been too easy, and any day, Dehazku could be coming for him...The thought of meeting the elder again fills Val with fear. No doubt Dehazku would't hesitate to use Val like a cog in some greater machine...But screw that, he'd figure this werewolf stuff out on his own. Besides, his mom's a pretty chill lady, she'd understand...<br /> <br /> <br /> Tribe: Vrikodara Jata (Get of Fenris)<br /> Auspice: Ragabash<br /> Breed : Homid <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","user":"Al-Haleem","date":". 09-17-2014, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T16:17:58-07:00","id":269584,"title":"","content":"What is the status with this game? Has anyone else heard from NutiketAiel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T16:50:23-07:00","id":269597,"title":"","content":"No, not a word. His profile says he's online right now, but he didn't post anything new on the forum since September 16th. Maybe real life got in the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T05:20:01-07:00","id":270070,"title":"","content":"The game is still on. First off, let me apologize for my absence. I've been working 12-16 hour days every day since 9/3, and when I wasn't working, I was spending my free time with my Grandmother, who has been in the hospital. I should have at least shot you guys a message; failing to do so was very inconsiderate of me, and for that I apologize. That being said, my work schedule is easing up (I actually have the whole day off tomorrow), and my Grandmother should be released from the hospital this evening, or tomorrow morning at the latest. Right now I am going to go to sleep, as I just got home from a 14 hour shift. This afternoon I am going to visit my Grandmother. But this evening, and tomorrow, I will be back, and I intend to kick this pregame into high gear. In the meantime, everyone who's still here, thanks for bearing with me. Can I get a roll call? Everyone who is still around, please check in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T05:48:16-07:00","id":270086,"title":"","content":"I'm still here. Don't worry, take care of your Grandmother, it's way more important than a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T08:19:21-07:00","id":270133,"title":"","content":"I'm definitely still here, and ready to be the worst...er BEST Ragabash ever! And I admit I was a bit worried about you Nutiket, if the concern of an anonymous internet dweller means anything to you. I sincerely hope your grandma's okay, and life in general eases up on you. May we yet see the Summer Land, and bask in Gaia's glory...I'm already in a werewolfey mood, that's how excited I am.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T15:22:24-07:00","id":270421,"title":"","content":"Still here,<br /> <br /> I figured you just had some personal stuff, I hope your days get easier.<br /> <br /> -Cheers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T18:16:28-07:00","id":270519,"title":"","content":"I'm still here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T18:53:14-07:00","id":270525,"title":"","content":"I'm here, as well. Take care, we understand that real life's gotta come first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T09:17:49-07:00","id":270853,"title":"","content":"Glad you're all still with me. :-) Thank you so much for your understanding. Thank you also for expressing concern about my grandmother; she is being released from the hospital this afternoon, and she is well.<br /> <br /> I spoke to Camilla before my work and family life imploded- he will not be joining us for the time being. Too much going on in his personal life (I know how that feels). We still have five players, which is a great number. However, I did say my maximum was six, so if someone else applies in the next few days, I'll probably accept them. However, I'm not going to delay the game any longer for recruitment purposes. This means that if any of you guys know someone who's looking to join a werewolf game, there's still room for one more. ;-)<br /> <br /> Deathmatch, Marmelade, Markers and Echoes, as soon as I'm done this post, I'm going to wrap up the private setting background posts for each of you and send them to you by PM. These will take the form of IC exposition from one (or more) characters from your characters' sept or tribe. In cases where the character background includes a mentor, it'll be him/her. I'm going for a feel like the tribebooks, particularly the exposition sections that are written in the style of an experienced tribe member teaching a cub. Remember, like the initial setting information post, this information can be considered basic IC knowledge for your character; however, OOC, I am not confirming its accuracy! In some cases, the mentor will be speaking on subjects they have incomplete knowledge of. In other cases, they will be passing on rumors or speculation. Some of the information will be filtered by their own interpretation and frame of reference. And even mentors lie sometimes, if they feel the need. On the other hand, some of the information will be totally accurate. It's up to all of you to decide what your characters believe (especially when the information from these posts contradicts the general knowledge post). We can go over them as needed, in case anything is unclear, and it is my hope and intention to have character sheet templates and character creation rules posted by tomorrow (they just need a little tweaking).<br /> <br /> However, first I want to take a minute and address Haleem's character concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=258941#post258941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, awesome, I actually wanted to play a Ragabash character! I can write out a little biography if that helps, apologies if you weren't looking for that:<br /> <br /> Narasimha-Vallabha (Or Val as he prefers to be called) was born in New York to an eccentric named Natasha Narula, a screenwriting lecturer at New York University. His father died of heart complications when he was only seven, so he was left to his mother's rather lax child-rearing methods, which consisted of letting him do whatever the hell he liked. Always interested in his Indian heritage, Val studied the Vedas as well as Sanskrit, and can rattle off shlokas with surprising ease. Sometimes they're even accurate.<br /> <br /> Just before entering university, his mother received a letter inviting her and her son to a reunion at the Narula clan's estate in Utter Pradesh. Natasha had no interest in going, but she was unusually insistent that her son attend. Ever-eager for new experiences, Val agreed.<br /> <br /> He arrived in a country unlike anything he'd imagined. No amount of Bollywood had prepared him for how different life in Hindustan was. Reaching his family's serene <i>hawaili</i> was something of a relief, and his relatives were infinitely gracious despite his awful Hindi. They arranged a magnificent dinner in his honor, and were positively obsequious. Rather an ostentatious affair for the prodigal son of the family's black sheep. In fact, everything was a bit suspicious...No one would stop smiling. And then there was this damn ringing in his ears, and then...<br /> <br /> He awoke to darkness, and an unholy thirst. A gentle, bearded face appeared at his side and offered him a glass of...something. Val drank it without thinking and returned to oblivion.<br /> <br /> Val discovered the gravity of his predicament when next he woke. He'd been left at the bottom of a deep, dry well. During the day, the well was sealed, but at night, he could gaze up at the magnificent star-studded heavens, and the moon, brighter then he'd ever seen it. His only companion was the bearded man, who appeared when he awoke, and offered him his only sustenance, something he called 'soma'.<br /> <br /> And Val dreamt, of days past, of gods and heroes, and wolves, always wolves. Moons slipped by alongside time, until existence itself seemed so little and insignificant. On a night of perfect, unbroken darkness, he stared into a beautiful abyss, and was filled with the very essence of life. Howling out in ecstasy, Val knew nothing but the rush of blood in his veins, and the frantic beat of his heart. Claws tore at stone walls, terrible teeth gnashed, and Val wanted to kill...And the bearded man appeared again, and Val flexed his talons, hungry for blood, but then the bearded man became something...<i>more</i>.<br /> <br /> Val entered a hidden world, he was one of the Chosen, or so he was told. The bearded man, named Dehazku, instructed him in the ancient arts of his tribe, stripping Val of his old name, his very identity, and preparing him for a life dedicated to his new family, Dehazku called them the 'Vrikodara Jata'. Dehazku, following some arcane series of astrological predictions had determined Val would be born with the mark of the moon, and was destined for great things. With manic eyes, Dehazku told Val told he was pure and fit for breeding, that he would lead his tribe to a new golden age, that he would help retake Hindustan from blood-drinking vetala and wicked demons who took the form of tigers. Quickly determining that Dehazku was slightly nuts, Val thought only of escape, and his poor mother, who'd given birth to a monster.<br /> <br /> So he fled, making for New York, but Val is deeply worried that Dehazku simply let him go, as a sort of test, it'd all been too easy, and any day, Dehazku could be coming for him...The thought of meeting the elder again fills Val with fear. No doubt Dehazku would't hesitate to use Val like a cog in some greater machine...But screw that, he'd figure this werewolf stuff out on his own. Besides, his mom's a pretty chill lady, she'd understand...<br /> <br /> <br /> Tribe: Vrikodara Jata (Get of Fenris)<br /> Auspice: Ragabash<br /> Breed : Homid<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>First off, I like the concept. It's fairly unique. :-) I have to warn you, though, that I have limited knowledge of Indian culture. Well, I know more on the subject than an average American, to be sure, but I'm hardly an expert. For example, I know what the Vedas are, and what Sanskrit is, and what Soma was (as much as anyone knows what Soma was, since I don't think historians agree on its composition), and where Uttar Pradesh is, but I had no idea until I went googling what a shloka is. This means that I may occasionally need to ask you for clarification of certain points. The nice part about a PbP game, as opposed to a straight tabletop game, however, is that I can take a little time for research as needed between posts.<br /> <br /> Secondly, this game is set in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delaware_Valley\" target=\"_blank\">Delaware Valley</a> (which includes the Philadelphia Metropolitan Area), not New York City. Take a look at the setting post, way at the beginning of this thread, for more information. So, if your character is heading back home to NYC, he'll be well out of our area. There are a few simple solutions. First off, Val and his mom could easily be from Philadelphia rather than NYC. If not, however, we need a reason for Val to be in the Delaware Valley rather than New York City. Perhaps he feared leading Dehazku back to his mother (or feared going back to her himself as a monster), and wanted to go somewhere else for her protection? Or perhaps he was afraid for himself, and chose not to go back to NYC where he would be more easily found?<br /> <br /> Thirdly, I am unfamiliar with the Vrikodara Jata; I have never heard of a Get of Fenris off-shoot in India. Are they from a book that I am not familiar with, or are they your own creation? If they're your own creation, that's fine, but we'll need to discuss some details so I know where to go with them in the story. Also, if you could translate the term for me...<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":". 10-02-2014, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T10:35:51-07:00","id":270905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=270853#post270853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Deathmatch, Marmelade, Markers and Echoes, as soon as I'm done this post, I'm going to wrap up the private setting background posts for each of you and send them to you by PM. These will take the form of IC exposition from one (or more) characters from your characters' sept or tribe. In cases where the character background includes a mentor, it'll be him/her. I'm going for a feel like the tribebooks, particularly the exposition sections that are written in the style of an experienced tribe member teaching a cub. Remember, like the initial setting information post, this information can be considered basic IC knowledge for your character; however, OOC, I am not confirming its accuracy! In some cases, the mentor will be speaking on subjects they have incomplete knowledge of. In other cases, they will be passing on rumors or speculation. Some of the information will be filtered by their own interpretation and frame of reference. And even mentors lie sometimes, if they feel the need. On the other hand, some of the information will be totally accurate. It's up to all of you to decide what your characters believe (especially when the information from these posts contradicts the general knowledge post). We can go over them as needed, in case anything is unclear, and it is my hope and intention to have character sheet templates and character creation rules posted by tomorrow (they just need a little tweaking).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. Can we answer to the PM IC if we have some questions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T10:38:04-07:00","id":270908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=270905#post270905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice. Can we answer to the PM IC if we have some questions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but keep them brief. I don't want to turn it into a whole prelude session. I do it this way so that I can get across a lot of information without having to take time to run a full prelude, which can be time consuming in an online setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T10:45:39-07:00","id":270943,"title":"","content":"'kay. That's what I was worried about. I'll wait for the PM now. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T10:52:29-07:00","id":270947,"title":"","content":"I'm going to send them one at a time, as I finish them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T08:10:51-07:00","id":271627,"title":"","content":"Hey Jim! I'm glad my character concept wasn't too out there. Don't worry, I'm aware where the game's set, I just wanted to get my character's back story down. And I like your idea of Val deciding at the last minute that Dehazku would come for him in New York, so he ends up in Delaware out of fear for himself and his mom. I wanted my character to be a bit of an outsider, which is why I choose a location so far removed from the game's setting. I hope it didn't mess anything up. <br /> As for the Vrikodara Jata, its a name I invented. I wanted to use the sourcebooks, but I couldn't find anything on India. Anyway, Vrikodara means 'wolf-bellied' and is a title for Bhima, a character from the Mahabharata famed for his ferocity and strength. Jata means brood or family. So it literally translates as 'Brood of the Wolf-bellied One'. It's the closest I could get to an Indian Get of Fenris, not many wolves in Hindu mythology sadly. <br /> <br /> -Haleem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T10:57:49-07:00","id":271653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=271627#post271627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Jim! I'm glad my character concept wasn't too out there. Don't worry, I'm aware where the game's set, I just wanted to get my character's back story down. And I like your idea of Val deciding at the last minute that Dehazku would come for him in New York, so he ends up in Delaware out of fear for himself and his mom. I wanted my character to be a bit of an outsider, which is why I choose a location so far removed from the game's setting. I hope it didn't mess anything up.<br /> As for the Vrikodara Jata, its a name I invented. I wanted to use the sourcebooks, but I couldn't find anything on India. Anyway, Vrikodara means 'wolf-bellied' and is a title for Bhima, a character from the Mahabharata famed for his ferocity and strength. Jata means brood or family. So it literally translates as 'Brood of the Wolf-bellied One'. It's the closest I could get to an Indian Get of Fenris, not many wolves in Hindu mythology sadly.<br /> <br /> -Haleem</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, cool. Well, let's start with some basics. Has Val been in contact with his mother at all since his escape? Even if he hasn't seen her, has he called her to say that he was alright, or sent a text, or an email, or a letter or some such? Or has he completely avoided any kind of contact with her? Whichever he did, what was the reasoning behind that decision?<br /> <br /> How old is Val, exactly? The initial post was a little ambiguous on that point.<br /> <br /> Now, the game is going to begin with the characters going through their Rite of Passage together. This means that, at some point, Val is going to have to come into contact with some of the local Garou prior to the game beginning. There are a million and one ways this can have happened. Perhaps Val got caught up in a fight with or between one of the many supernatural factions in the Delaware Valley. Or perhaps a kinfolk met Val, realized what he was and guided him to the local garou (or the other way around, putting the local garou onto Val's trail). Or the same role could have been filled by a spirit. Like I said, a million possibilities. Have you given any thought to what Val's introduction to the local Garou would be?<br /> <br /> Now, most Garou in this setting are attached, at least loosely, to one particular Sept. The pack, once formed, will represent the region as a whole and include members from several individual septs, but the individual pack members still have ties to individual septs, for the most part. This is partly for story reasons, as it gives them a certain set of NPCs to interact with regularly and gives me a chance to expound on the setting. It is also for practical in character reasons- having a home base and a sept structure you can turn to at need is very valuable for garou, especially young garou. If you haven't already, read the setting information at the beginning of this thread (it's essential reading for this game, actually, so if you haven't done so yet, you need to do so now before we can move any further with character creation; I know it's long, sorry).<br /> <br /> Now, as you can see, there is one Get of Fenris dominated caern in the region, the Germantown Volunteers Sept, so that is a possibility. However, that's not the only option; there are several open and multi-tribal septs where Val could have found acceptance, too. For example, if Val was living on the streets when he first arrived in the region, the Bone Gnawers of the Sept of Dockyard Miracles might have sheltered him. Or, perhaps he went to a charitable organization looking for help with the basic necessities and ended up being put in touch with the Children of Gaia at the Sept of Friends. If he had a little money, he might have been looking for a discreet place to rent a room for a while and blundered into the Glass Walker Society Hill Sept. Or whatever- plenty of options. Do any of these jump out at you?<br /> <br /> As for the Vrikodara Jata, there are two ways we can go. You and I can work out some of the details of their society, history and goals together ahead of time. Or, I can work it out myself privately, and you can discover it during the course of play as your character finds out. After all, he probably doesn't know much about this group. They kidnapped him, drugged him, induced his first change, and then he escaped. Not a lot of time in there for deep cultural learning. Which method would you prefer?<br /> <br /> Do you have any questions for me so far, about the game itself or the setting?<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T09:51:39-07:00","id":273965,"title":"","content":"Hi Jim! Many apologies for not replying sooner, I\u2019ve been travelling and my schedule\u2019s a bit disordered. Anyway, to answer your questions:<br /> <br /> Val\u2019s Mom: Val returned to New York and met up with his mother. However he couldn\u2019t quite work out how to say \u2018I think I\u2019m a werewolf\u2019 in a tactful manner. Furthermore, he was filled with a creeping dread that Dehazku was closing in on him. The thought of endangering his mother terrified Val, so he stole some of her money and used it to get as far away from home as he could. He knew it\u2019d leave his mom distraught, but it was better than the alternative. Val has a vivid imagination, if Dehazku confronts his mother, things will get messy, and he\u2019ll never forgive himself if she\u2019s harmed.<br /> <br /> Val\u2019s Age: Val is 17 going on 18.<br /> <br /> Val\u2019s Connection with Delaware Valley: Val arrives quite confused, he still doesn\u2019t understand his new \u2018condition\u2019 and apart from avoiding Dehazku, his greatest desire is to learn more of his furry alter-ego. Val scours the seedier side of town, hoping to encounter a fellow supernatural. He has an instinctual feeling that he\u2019ll no one when he sees them. At a dive bar, Val is approached by a mysterious man who claims he knows what he is. This man, Malakai, offers to explain the secrets of Val\u2019s new existence. Although he\u2019s nervous, Val is excited at the prospect of knowledge, and meeting a werewolf. It helps that Malakai is handsome, in a hard-bitten sort of way. Over several weeks, Malakai falls into the role of mentor, weaving a complex cosmology that boggles Val\u2019s mind. Unfortunately, Malakai is a Black Spiral Dancer, and Val soon believes he exists to serve the Wyrm, a benevolent entity that seeks to annihilate the current corrupt world, and create a paradise in its place. A bit out there, but a more palatable philosophy than Dehazku\u2019s fevered ranting\u2019s. After some time, Malakai decides Val is ready to be inducted into the \u2018family\u2019.<br /> <br /> He takes Val to a deserted location, where he introduces him to other servants of the Wyrm. Val\u2019s slightly unsure of things at this point, but he\u2019s come too far to give up his search for answers. As the Black Spirals begin a ceremony to enfold Val in the Wyrm\u2019s embrace, a pack of Garou attack. They slay some of the Dancers, but the rest, along with Malakai, flee. Val, too slow to run for it, is soon the awkward centre of attention. The Garou are divided. Some think Val has been tainted and should be destroyed; others are less convinced of his corruption. The deciding vote comes from a Child of Gaia, Sunchaser. She vouches for Val, and offers to take him under her wing. Confused, and with no one else to turn to, Val reluctantly agrees.<br /> <br /> Val\u2019s Sept: Sunchaser is a member of the Sept of Friends, and welcomes Val to their number. She\u2019s fascinated by the lost cub, and tries to coax out information of his past, to no avail. Val spins increasingly elaborate lies, and while Sunchaser doesn\u2019t buy them, she accepts Val\u2019s desire for privacy. Sunchaser teaches Val Gaian philosophy, but at this point, he\u2019s sceptical. After getting versions of the truth from Dehazku, Malakai and now Sunchaser, Val doesn\u2019t know what to believe. Gaia? How do you know she\u2019s real? The Triat? It sounds like a rip-off of the Hindu Trimurti. And now the Wyrm\u2019s bad? Can\u2019t anyone make up their mind? Through it all, Val keeps his silence, planning his next move, dreaming of escape.<br /> <br /> Vrikodara Jata: I had some vague ideas on the sub-tribe\u2019s nature, but it sounds more fun if you work out the details, if you\u2019re willing. Go wild! My only request is you make their philosophy quite alien to the average Western Garou. I can\u2019t wait to see what you come up with.<br /> <br /> So there it is. I hope it wasn\u2019t too long-winded, but you inspired me. No questions yet, you\u2019ve been very thorough with your information. And I\u2019d also like to thank you for putting so much effort into this whole deal, I\u2019m truly impressed.<br /> <br /> PS: If you don\u2019t think Val\u2019s a viable character, I had a second option. An Abomination named Ebon Moondark, doomed to walk the earth, lamenting his cruel fate. He excels at soliloquys expounding on his bleak existence, contemplating the nature of life, waxing lyrical on the night\u2019s beauty etc. etc. Possesses several level six Gifts, which he learnt on the internet (vampiric werewolves have lots of free time) and has a Grand Klaive with a ten page backstory I\u2019m more than willing to share. He has purple eyes, and is terribly attractive (but thinks he\u2019s hideous) and sparkles under electric light (so he doesn\u2019t go out much). Spoiler: He\u2019s actually Caine in disguise. Shhh. I don\u2019t like to brag, but he\u2019s a pretty darn amazing character. I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if he starred in his own Tribe-novel. (Those are still a thing right?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","user":"Al-Haleem","date":". 10-06-2014, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T11:04:25-07:00","id":274044,"title":"","content":"So, Al-Haleem, hope you don't mind my input, but why exactly is Val still in the Get of Fenris? Does he wish to change tribe? Is he afraid to do so? Because as far as I understood it, he's feeling from Dekahzu who seems to be one of their leader (at least the indian branch of the tribe). I don't quite understand why he's still a Get.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https:/