9,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=273965#post273965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Jim! Many apologies for not replying sooner, I\u2019ve been travelling and my schedule\u2019s a bit disordered. Anyway, to answer your questions:<br /> <br /> Val\u2019s Mom: Val returned to New York and met up with his mother. However he couldn\u2019t quite work out how to say \u2018I think I\u2019m a werewolf\u2019 in a tactful manner. Furthermore, he was filled with a creeping dread that Dehazku was closing in on him. The thought of endangering his mother terrified Val, so he stole some of her money and used it to get as far away from home as he could. He knew it\u2019d leave his mom distraught, but it was better than the alternative. Val has a vivid imagination, if Dehazku confronts his mother, things will get messy, and he\u2019ll never forgive himself if she\u2019s harmed.<br /> <br /> Val\u2019s Age: Val is 17 going on 18.<br /> <br /> Val\u2019s Connection with Delaware Valley: Val arrives quite confused, he still doesn\u2019t understand his new \u2018condition\u2019 and apart from avoiding Dehazku, his greatest desire is to learn more of his furry alter-ego. Val scours the seedier side of town, hoping to encounter a fellow supernatural. He has an instinctual feeling that he\u2019ll no one when he sees them. At a dive bar, Val is approached by a mysterious man who claims he knows what he is. This man, Malakai, offers to explain the secrets of Val\u2019s new existence. Although he\u2019s nervous, Val is excited at the prospect of knowledge, and meeting a werewolf. It helps that Malakai is handsome, in a hard-bitten sort of way. Over several weeks, Malakai falls into the role of mentor, weaving a complex cosmology that boggles Val\u2019s mind. Unfortunately, Malakai is a Black Spiral Dancer, and Val soon believes he exists to serve the Wyrm, a benevolent entity that seeks to annihilate the current corrupt world, and create a paradise in its place. A bit out there, but a more palatable philosophy than Dehazku\u2019s fevered ranting\u2019s. After some time, Malakai decides Val is ready to be inducted into the \u2018family\u2019.<br /> <br /> He takes Val to a deserted location, where he introduces him to other servants of the Wyrm. Val\u2019s slightly unsure of things at this point, but he\u2019s come too far to give up his search for answers. As the Black Spirals begin a ceremony to enfold Val in the Wyrm\u2019s embrace, a pack of Garou attack. They slay some of the Dancers, but the rest, along with Malakai, flee. Val, too slow to run for it, is soon the awkward centre of attention. The Garou are divided. Some think Val has been tainted and should be destroyed; others are less convinced of his corruption. The deciding vote comes from a Child of Gaia, Sunchaser. She vouches for Val, and offers to take him under her wing. Confused, and with no one else to turn to, Val reluctantly agrees.<br /> <br /> Val\u2019s Sept: Sunchaser is a member of the Sept of Friends, and welcomes Val to their number. She\u2019s fascinated by the lost cub, and tries to coax out information of his past, to no avail. Val spins increasingly elaborate lies, and while Sunchaser doesn\u2019t buy them, she accepts Val\u2019s desire for privacy. Sunchaser teaches Val Gaian philosophy, but at this point, he\u2019s sceptical. After getting versions of the truth from Dehazku, Malakai and now Sunchaser, Val doesn\u2019t know what to believe. Gaia? How do you know she\u2019s real? The Triat? It sounds like a rip-off of the Hindu Trimurti. And now the Wyrm\u2019s bad? Can\u2019t anyone make up their mind? Through it all, Val keeps his silence, planning his next move, dreaming of escape.<br /> <br /> Vrikodara Jata: I had some vague ideas on the sub-tribe\u2019s nature, but it sounds more fun if you work out the details, if you\u2019re willing. Go wild! My only request is you make their philosophy quite alien to the average Western Garou. I can\u2019t wait to see what you come up with.<br /> <br /> So there it is. I hope it wasn\u2019t too long-winded, but you inspired me. No questions yet, you\u2019ve been very thorough with your information. And I\u2019d also like to thank you for putting so much effort into this whole deal, I\u2019m truly impressed.<br /> <br /> PS: If you don\u2019t think Val\u2019s a viable character, I had a second option. An Abomination named Ebon Moondark, doomed to walk the earth, lamenting his cruel fate. He excels at soliloquys expounding on his bleak existence, contemplating the nature of life, waxing lyrical on the night\u2019s beauty etc. etc. Possesses several level six Gifts, which he learnt on the internet (vampiric werewolves have lots of free time) and has a Grand Klaive with a ten page backstory I\u2019m more than willing to share. He has purple eyes, and is terribly attractive (but thinks he\u2019s hideous) and sparkles under electric light (so he doesn\u2019t go out much). Spoiler: He\u2019s actually Caine in disguise. Shhh. I don\u2019t like to brag, but he\u2019s a pretty darn amazing character. I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if he starred in his own Tribe-novel. (Those are still a thing right?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, since your backup plan is apparently an Abomination that's secretly Caine, I guess we have to be OK with Val. :-P<br /> <br /> Let's see. I'm OK with most of this.<br /> <br /> I have one more question about Val's relationship with his mother, at this time. When he returned to NYC and saw her, the very first question she asked was &quot;How was your trip?&quot; How did he respond to that?<br /> <br /> I can work with Malakai; in fact, he fits the archetype of a BSD NPC I already had in the setting, so I can just use Malakai as that character's name. I can similarly work with Sunchaser and integrate that character into the Sept of Friends. She's a Rank 3 Homid Philodox, the Sept's Master of the Challenge, for the record. Unless that conflicts with what you had in mind for her? I can work with you on this to some degree.<br /> <br /> I'm also cool with Val having a significant degree of confusion about the cosmology and culture. This seems like it would be well expressed through the Twisted Upbringing flaw, and I urge you to take that flaw when the time comes.<br /> <br /> I'm a little concerned about Val's continued desire to escape, however. It will be difficult to incorporate him into a pack if he is constantly trying to flee, and while I find Val's story interesting, I don't want the chronicle to be totally derailed by having to pull out of whatever adventure they are in so the pack can track down Val. I especially don't want that to happen more than once. I'm sure he's still uneasy and unsure of these new Garou, but I'm hoping that Sunchaser's compassion impressed him enough that he's at least willing to give them the benefit of the doubt, and then hopefully once he's bonded with a pack after the Rite of Passage, he'll feel better about staying. A constant desire to flee, however, would be a problem.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to know a little more about why he's a member of the Get of Fenris. I mean, he's descended from the Vrikodara Jata, and they are a distant camp (or sub-tribe or whatever) of the Get, and genetics does play a roll in the choice, but it's also a spiritual matter, far more than genetics. A cub can choose another tribe; it's not at all uncommon (for example, take a look at the backstory for Scott Cavendish, Deathmatch's character, who is a Stargazer of Silver Fang descent, or Marmelade's character, Geoff Bolen, who is of mixed Fianna/Child of Gaia descent and chose the Children of Gaia). So, did he choose to become a Fenrir? Or did it just kind of work out that way because of his genetics and temperament? If the former, why did he make that choice? If the latter, what about him makes him fit in with the Get? Did something in his mind or spirit impress Great Fenris? How do you envision his relationship with the rest of his tribe after his rite of passage? Note that I'm not trying to get you to change Val's tribe- I just want to understand more about the reasons behind the choice, both IC and OOC.<br /> <br /> I am perfectly willing to fill in the details about the Vrikodara Jata. I have a few ideas in mind already, including how to integrate them into the plot. Don't worry, they will be fairly alien by the standards of the Western Concordiat. You (and the rest of the pack) will have opportunities to learn more about them during the course of play.<br /> <br /> A few more questions to think about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> What is Val's living situation? Is he on the streets? Is he sleeping in the Sept (this would be a temporary situation, as the Sept of Friends is quite small and doesn't have a place for garou to live long-term)? Is he staying in Sunchaser's apartment? Is he in a shelter? Does he have his own place? If he has his own place, is he paying for it with the money he stole from his Mom until that runs out, or does he have some other way of getting income?<br /> <br /> Besides his Mom's money, did he bring anything with him from home when he fled?<br /> <br /> What are his feelings towards Malakai at this point? For example, if Malakai were to show up, right now, and offer to &quot;rescue&quot; Val from the Children of Gaia, would Val go with him? If not, would he try to fight Malakai, or call the other garou to fight Malakai? Or would he refuse to go with the BSD, but not alert the others to the intrusion? I'm not saying this is going to happen, I'm just trying to get you to think about Val's mindset, and I'm trying to get a feel for it myself.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ah, I see Marmelade Ninja'd me. We both do ask basically the same question, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":".  Ninja'd 10-06-2014, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T08:13:46-07:00","id":274729,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve been pondering your questions, and have settled on some tentative answers. Here goes:<br /> <br /> Val\u2019s mom: Keeping in mind Natasha\u2019s eccentricity and hatred of all things serious, here\u2019s how the conversation went:<br /> \u201cHow was your trip?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood\u2026It was\u2026Good.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCome on! I want details! Juicy ones!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay\u2026I got kidnapped by relatives, force-fed some godawful concoction, and I turned into a werewolf.\u201d<br /> <br /> Pause<br /> <br /> \u201cKidnapped by relatives? Must have been the Dhawans. I told you not to trust Punjabis. And now you're a werewolf? Does it have anything to do with that Furry Fandom thing? I read about it online.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026Nevermind. Can we go to that shady Italian place for dinner?\u201d<br /> <br /> Despite her levity, Natasha suspects something unpleasant happened to her son in India. Unfortunately, before she could push for more information, he fled.<br /> <br /> Val and \u2018tactical withdrawals\u2019: Val\u2019s desire for escape is more metaphysical than anything else. He feels trapped by his new existence, and searches for that one moment of blinding revelation when all becomes clear. He considers his current life with Sunchaser a temporary aberration, soon; he\u2019ll know the Truth, whatever it is. As long as Val has loyal packmates at his side, he won\u2019t flee danger (except if he\u2019s facing Dehazku). In fact, he\u2019ll probably appreciate being a member of a pack. Safety in numbers.<br /> <br /> Val and Sunchaser: I\u2019ll let you handle the mechanical stuff regarding Sunchaser\u2019s character. As for his relationship with her, it could be better. Val\u2019s currently occupying her couch, and while he appreciates it, he wishes she\u2019d stop with all the pseudo-philosophy. He finds her ideals painfully maudlin, all that claptrap about peace and unity and unicorns, it\u2019s sweet enough to give him diabetes. Despite his constant lip, Sunchaser drives on, perhaps unwisely. A less patient Garou would\u2019ve tossed Val into a nest of Banes already\u2026<br /> <br /> Val and Great Fenris: Now this question set my brain working. I\u2019ll divide my answer into \u2018In Character\u2019 reasons and \u2018Out of Character\u2019 reasons. Prepare yourself, much reading follows:<br /> <br /> In Character: On the surface, Val is the least suitable Fenrir ever. He\u2019s scrawny, prefers words to weapons, and he can\u2019t quite work up a blood lust, although he\u2019s really trying on that count. However, Val may be closer to Fenris\u2019 heart than he realises. When he underwent the First Change, such a torrent of long-supressed rage was unleashed he sickens to recall it. Dehazku saw something in him, and he\u2019s terrified to discover just what it is.<br /> <br /> But how will his Tribe react? They\u2019ll likely dismiss him as a mewling weakling. Which is exactly the wrong (right?) thing to do. Val fled Dehazku precisely because the elder was disturbingly insistent he join the Jata. Now, with the Western segment of the Tribe laughing him off, Val\u2019s incandescent. He resents having his fate decided by others, and he loathes having assumptions made about his character, especially if they\u2019re close to the bone. Faced by his Tribe\u2019s disdain, Val is deeply driven to prove their skewed assessment of him wrong, by any means.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, although he\u2019d never admit it, Val possesses the infamous Fenrir intolerance. He has an irrational hatred of absolutes, and his knee-jerk defiance of Sunchaser is in part motivated by a refusal to accept her world view. Val plays the devil\u2019s advocate by default. Even if he secretly agrees with someone\u2019s ideals, he\u2019ll insist on picking holes in their beliefs. Naturally, there is the genetic aspect. The twisted branches of Val\u2019s family tree bend beneath the weight of glorious ancestors, warriors of great renown, and they\u2019ve left their mark upon him. While Val would balk at the notion that he\u2019s defined by his past, he cannot escape the memory of his First Change, and the dark part of him that enjoyed it. Perhaps Great Fenris (or Vrikodara) knows Val better than he knows himself, a chilling notion\u2026<br /> <br /> Out of Character: In truth, I can\u2019t stand the Get of Fenris. To me, they\u2019re the least interesting Tribe. It\u2019s just a bunch of thugs comparing Klaive sizes, flexing their biceps and channelling Robert E. Howard at his most unintellectual. So I wanted to prove the stereotype wrong, to create an \u2018anti-Fenrir\u2019 for want of a better term. Val might not be a sword-swinging Conan rip-off, but in a subtle way, he embodies Fenrir ideals. Fenris respects strength. But can\u2019t strength be found within; found in love and unbreakable spirit? Fenris respects courage. But there are many ways to be courageous. Accepting oneself, being true to oneself, surely that\u2019s the most courageous act of all. Fenris respects skill in battle. But battles take many forms. Wars can be won with words, with guile and intelligence. Not all battles are fought with steel.<br /> <br /> With all this in mind, I don\u2019t think Val would fit into any other Tribe. Surely Great Fenris\u2019 creed is not so narrow; surely his warriors wear many masks. I want to explore these ideas through Val, and maybe I\u2019ll come to see the Get in an entirely new light.<br /> <br /> Val\u2019s living situation: As mentioned above, he\u2019s staying with Sunchaser, and it\u2019ll be interesting to see which one of them Frenzy\u2019s first. Apart from his mom\u2019s misappropriated money, which he feels guilty spending, Sunchaser provides him with a bit of cash. Other than the clothes on his back and a bag containing sundry apparel, Val owns a well-loved copy of the Mahabharata and an intensely non-magical amulet he wears at all times.<br /> <br /> Val\u2019s relationship with Malakai: It\u2019s complicated. He misses the werewolf\u2019s company in a way; he was far less pedantic than Sunchaser, and easier on the eyes. Although Sunchaser\u2019s explained Malakai is a servant of the Wyrm, which is a bad thing, Val isn\u2019t buying it. He sees the conflict between the Gaian Garou and the Black Spiral Dancers as a subjective religious dispute. Val knows that in India today, there are still deadly riots sparked by religious or cultural factors, so why should it be any different for werewolves? Malakai can\u2019t be evil, surely not. Sunchaser\u2019s just demonising a doctrinal opponent, no doubt. If Malakai were to turn up, grin lasciviously, and offer to take Val away, he\u2019d probably go. But he\u2019d have a lot of questions, and he might not like the answers\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","user":"Al-Haleem","date":". 10-07-2014, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T11:39:16-07:00","id":276529,"title":"","content":"When I was talking about him running away, I didn't mean running from battle; I meant more along the lines of him trying to leave the pack and strike out on his own. I am glad that will not be an issue.<br /> <br /> I definitely find your ideas for the Get of Fenris to be interesting, and would like to see how they play out. I would like Val to have at least one contact, even if it is a tenuous one, among the local Get of Fenris so that he can have at least some ability to connect to the tribe without just popping over to their caern and saying &quot;here I am&quot; if he needs to talk to them, but I have an NPC in mind for this and will introduce you to him when I send you the private setting information for Val.<br /> <br /> For now, we seem to be pretty good to start out. Is there any other aspect of the character you wished to discuss?<br /> <br /> For that matter, does anyone else have anything about Val that they want to get into, or any advice or questions for Haleem? I enjoy the way our group worked cooperatively on character creation earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T12:55:00-07:00","id":276593,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I don't have anything else to ask to Val. I'm just curious to see how he will react when he'll have to form a pack with a Children of Gaia. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T06:07:24-07:00","id":277154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/244557-recruitment-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=276593#post276593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I don't have anything else to ask to Val. I'm just curious to see how he will react when he'll have to form a pack with a Children of Gaia. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Expect fireworks, constant back-chat and perhaps...Romance? I joke of course, it'll probably end in tears and general hysterics. Looking forward to it. And I'm interested to see how Val's Fenrir contact turns out. I have a feeling their relationship will be...complex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T07:35:07-07:00","id":277218,"title":"","content":"Well, Geoff <i>is</i> gay after all. But yeah, I wonder how long it's gonna take for him to be fed up with a passive-aggressive behaviour. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T18:38:35-07:00","id":284462,"title":"","content":"So... Where are we on this game? I'm really impatient for it to start!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T06:37:01-07:00","id":284908,"title":"","content":"You and me both! I just hope Jim hasn't met with an awful accident, then I'll feel like an ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T11:15:33-07:00","id":287845,"title":"","content":"No, no accident I'm afraid. Just more work.<br /> <br /> I just want to make one thing clear- these delays will not be a problem once we actually start. My work schedule is still going to be insane, but the problem right now is that typing these background posts takes a few hours each, involving a lot of cross-referencing between my notes (some of which are still hand-written) and my books. A normal reply to RP takes much less time, and is even something I can do from my phone while at work, for small things.<br /> <br /> Now, that being said, I have most of the day free today (finally), so I am going to finish up the last two background posts and send them out. I hope to have time to also polish up the character creation rules and have them posted immediately afterwards (and before I go into work at 2200), but if I don't, I promise that I will do them as soon as I get home from work in the morning (probably about 1000-ish), before sleep.<br /> <br /> So, in other words- no sleep until we're ready to start mechanical character creation. This I vow. ;-)<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T01:32:02-07:00","id":288419,"title":"","content":"Good grief, your work hours are crazy! Are you a member of an ancient conspiracy? An agent for a supernatural detective agency? Whatever it is, you have admirable willpower. Motivating myself to do the dishes is sometimes an epic mental struggle. Thanks for the update though, and I'm just glad nothing unpleasant happened to you. Besides work, that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T10:01:49-07:00","id":288652,"title":"","content":"OK, I have just sent the final background information packet. All five of you should have received yours by now via PM. If any of you did not receive your character's background knowledge packet, please let me know ASAP so I can resend.<br /> <br /> I will now complete the character creation mechanics, including associated House Rules, and the character sheet template. i will use both of these to create the OOC thread in the actual Play by Post section. As soon as they are up, I will edit this post to link to them from here.<br /> <br /> -Jim<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse\">OK, here is the link to the OOC discussion thread, which contains character creation rules and character sheet template. Let's keep new discussion in that thread, and save this thread for further recruitment, should it become necessary.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":". 10-21-2014, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T11:40:02-08:00","id":314729,"title":"","content":"We're about to officially start play day after tomorrow, so recruitment is now officially closed until further notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}